Is this, oh, hello, or is it hi there?
这是“哦，你好”，还是“嗨，你好”？

200
00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.370
Because, oh, you pivoted.
因为，哦，你转换话题了。

201
00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:49.330
It's all.
就这样。

202
00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:50.930
It's, oh, hello.
那个，哦，你好。

203
00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:51.830
Hi there.
你好呀。

204
00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:52.450
Hi there.
你好呀。

205
00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:54.130
Oh, good to see you again.
哦，很高兴再次见到你。

206
00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.390
Top of the morning to you.
早上好。

207
00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.070
That's right.
没错。

208
00:07:56.210 --> 00:08:00.810
Good to see you again, Mike Schur as Moe's, who we haven't seen in a real long time.
很高兴再次见到你，迈克·舒尔，也就是莫，我们好久没见他了。

209
00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:01.510
Yes.
是的。

210
00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

211
00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:03.410
Oh, is that section done?
哦，那部分结束了吗？

212
00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.350
That section's done.
那部分结束了。

213
00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:04.590
Okay.
好的。

214
00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.230
Oh, hello, hi there is done.
哦，你好，你好呀，结束了。

215
00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:06.830
Yes.
是的。

216
00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:08.050
And the goodbyes are done.
告别部分也结束了。

217
00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:08.310
Okay.
好的。

218
00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.630
In fact, I'm moving on to Fast Fact number two.
事实上，我要进入第二个快速事实了。

219
00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:11.990
Oh, let's do it.
哦，来吧。

220
00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.430
I'm calling Fast Fact number two, Reflections.
我把第二个快速事实称为“反思”。

221
00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.750
Oh, gosh.
哦，天哪。

222
00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.650
And you did like the whisper voice.
你确实喜欢那个耳语的声音。

223
00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:19.530
Reflections.
反思。

224
00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.250
Reflections with office ladies.
办公室女士的反思。

225
00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.190
We got a fan question from Allison W.
我们收到了来自德克萨斯州达拉斯市艾莉森·W的粉丝提问，

226
00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:26.070
in Dallas, Texas, who asked,
她问，

227
00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:31.890
now that you've watched eight seasons of the show, what is your favorite episode so far?
既然你们已经看了八季节目，到目前为止你们最喜欢哪一集？

228
00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:34.990
I thought that question might kick off our Reflections.
我觉得这个问题很适合开启我们的“反思”环节。

229
00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:37.710
Well, it's a fantastic question from Allison.
嗯，这是艾莉森提出的一个很棒的问题。

230
00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:39.230
What's up, Big D?
怎么了，达拉斯？

231
00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.250
Love, Dallas.
爱你们，达拉斯。

232
00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.550
Just thought I would just say that.
我只是想说一下。

233
00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:43.410
Shout out, Dallas.
向达拉斯致敬。

234
00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:44.490
Shout out, Dallas.
向达拉斯致敬。

235
00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.110
Gosh, Jenna, that's one of those thinking questions.
天哪，珍娜，这是一个需要深思的问题。

236
00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:49.810
I gave it some thought.
我思考了一下。

237
00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:50.830
I sent it to you.
我发给你了。

238
00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.370
We thought on it, Allison.
我们思考过了，艾莉森。

239
00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.470
We thought on it.
我们思考过了。

240
00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:54.130
We sure did.
我们确实思考了。

241
00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:58.070
It has been a really wild ride watching this show again.
重温这部剧真是一段疯狂的旅程。

242
00:08:58.230 --> 00:08:59.530
I've just loved it.
我真的很喜欢。

243
00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:03.550
I've really gained a deeper appreciation as a fan.
作为粉丝，我确实有了更深刻的体会。

244
00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:03.990
Yeah.
是啊。

245
00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:08.050
And I have to say, there are so many episodes that surprised me,
我不得不说，有很多集让我感到惊讶，

246
00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.370
that I had completely forgotten about.
我都完全忘记了。

247
00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:15.630
Or there were some that I totally changed my opinion about after we re-watched them.
或者有些集在重温之后，我的看法完全改变了。

248
00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:16.550
Give us an example.
给我们举个例子。

249
00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:17.430
Mafia.
《黑帮》那一集。

250
00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:18.430
Okay.
好的。

251
00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:22.490
I remember when we filmed it, I thought it was so broad and so silly.
我记得拍摄的时候，我觉得这太夸张、太傻了。

252
00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:22.890
Right.
没错。

253
00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.130
I thought, this is ridiculous.
我当时想，这简直荒唐。

254
00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.890
As a viewer, I just absolutely loved it.
但作为观众，我绝对非常喜欢它。

255
00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.030
It's one of my favorites now.
它现在是我最喜欢的剧集之一。

256
00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:29.410
Yeah.
是啊。

257
00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:32.590
I have really enjoyed watching the show evolve.
我真的很享受看着这部剧不断演变的过程。

258
00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:33.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

259
00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:39.310
But if I have to be honest, and this is what you do when you're reflecting.
但如果我要说实话，这就是你在回顾往事时会做的事。

260
00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:43.910
You just did that thing where you kind of looked over the top of your glasses a little.
你刚才又做了那个动作，就是那种稍微从眼镜上方看人的样子。

261
00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.390
Well, that's my lawyer look.
噢，那是我的律师表情。

262
00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:49.750
That's when you know I'm serious.
那是你该知道我认真起来的时候了。

263
00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:50.170
Okay.
好吧。

264
00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:50.730
Serious.
认真的。

265
00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:54.790
I thought season eight was a little clunky.
我觉得第八季有点笨拙。

266
00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:03.750
I know that we were trying to find our way after Steve left, and I think you can tell.
我知道史蒂夫离开后我们一直在努力寻找方向，我想这显而易见。

267
00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:10.530
Well, you're doing that thing where you say something you don't think is 100% going to be received well,
你看，你又在做那个动作了，当你说了些觉得可能不会被完全接受的话时，

268
00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:11.410
and you whisper it.
你就会压低声音说。

269
00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:12.650
Yeah.
是啊。

270
00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:15.190
I think here's your bless her heart.
我想这就是你的“愿上帝保佑它”。

271
00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:16.910
It's my bless her heart.
这是我的“愿上帝保佑它”。

272
00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.610
I mean, season eight, bless its heart.
我是说，第八季，愿上帝保佑它。

273
00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:20.670
Bless its heart.
愿上帝保佑它。

274
00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.410
I think it started well.
我觉得它开头不错。

275
00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.450
I would say I think it's ending, like, feeling like—
我想说的是，我觉得它结尾的时候，感觉像是——

276
00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:28.330
It ends strong.
结尾很强劲。

277
00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:29.250
Ends strong.
结尾很强劲。

278
00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:29.550
Yeah.
没错。

279
00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:31.770
Turf War and Free Family Portrait Studio.
《地盘之争》和《免费家庭肖像工作室》。

280
00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.710
We feel like we're back in the zone there, I think.
我觉得我们在那几集里找回了状态。

281
00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:39.790
But I think we took a real crazy detour around Pool Party.
但我觉得我们在《泳池派对》那一集绕了很大一个弯。

282
00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:40.970
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

283
00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:43.490
And then things got real kind of spotty.
然后情况就变得有点不稳定了。

284
00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:51.550
That said, I do think there are a lot of wonderful moments in season eight that are truly classic.
话虽如此，我确实认为第八季中有很多精彩的时刻，堪称经典。

285
00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:53.970
Big Preggs, Little Preggs.
《大孕妇，小孕妇》。

286
00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:54.690
Love that.
超爱那一集。

287
00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.470
Josh Groban in Garden Party.
《花园派对》里的乔什·格罗班。

288
00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.130
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

289
00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.290
Jerry Miner is Brandon.
杰瑞·迈纳饰演的布兰登。

290
00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:00.330
Perfect.
完美。

291
00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.550
Need him to be a series regular.
真希望他是常驻角色。

292
00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:03.650
Sad that he's not.
没能成为常驻真是遗憾。

293
00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:06.150
Also, we had unbelievable—
还有，我们有难以置信的——

294
00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.050
Unbelievable bedbugs.
难以置信的臭虫。

295
00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:08.990
Oh, bedbugs.
噢，臭虫。

296
00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.790
We had smug bedbug.
我们有自鸣得意的臭虫。

297
00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:11.390
Yes.
没错。

298
00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:15.770
I thought Jim's presentation at Test the Store, I'd forgotten about that.
我觉得吉姆在《测试商店》里的演讲很棒，我都快忘了那一幕了。

299
00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:16.570
Loved it.
超喜欢。

300
00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:21.510
But like I said last week, I really understand why people start over and rewatch.
但就像我上周说的，我真的很理解为什么人们会从头开始重温这部剧。

301
00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:28.710
I think that the show has evolved very subtly over the many seasons, and I really want to go back and see people from before.
我觉得这部剧在这么多季以来演变地非常微妙，我真的很想回去看看以前的人。

302
00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:30.330
I want to see Michael again.
我想再见到迈克尔。

303
00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:30.870
Yeah.
是啊。

304
00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.490
I want to see old Jim.
我想再见到以前的吉姆。

305
00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:36.830
I want to see Dwight and Angela and their romance unfold again.
我想再看一遍德怀特和安吉拉，看他们的恋情再次展开。

306
00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:37.710
Yeah.
是啊。

307
00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.310
That's such a good point.
你说得太对了。

308
00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:48.750
You know, like you said, I have this new appreciation for the show in a way that I didn't when we were filming it, even though I was a big fan of the show when we filmed it.
你知道，就像你说的，我对这部剧有了一种新的欣赏，这是我们在拍摄时所没有的，尽管我们在拍摄时也是这部剧的忠实粉丝。

309
00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:53.090
But now I have an appreciation of the fandom of the show.
但现在我对这部剧的粉丝群体有了新的认识。

310
00:11:53.510 --> 00:12:01.550
And what I mean by that is when we first started this rewatch, so many people would come up to us and tell us how many times they had watched the show all the way through.
我的意思是，当我们刚开始重温这部剧时，很多人走过来告诉我们他们把这部剧完整地看了多少遍。

311
00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.190
And it's many times.
而且是很多遍。

312
00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:06.170
I mean, you guys have really watched the show.
我是说，你们是真的把这部剧看进去了。

313
00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:14.090
And I realized there were so many episodes, I mean whole seasons, that I hadn't seen since they aired.
我意识到有太多集，我是说整整几季，自从播出后我就没再看过。

314
00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:14.570
Yeah.
是啊。

315
00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:21.010
So I have this new appreciation for the fandom because, like what you were just saying, we're coming to the end of this rewatch,
所以我对粉丝群体有了新的欣赏，因为就像你刚才说的，我们快要重温完了，

316
00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:24.830
and I find myself just so desperately wanting to go back to season one.
我发现自己非常渴望回到第一季。

317
00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:25.470
Me too.
我也是。

318
00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:29.310
It's emotional, and it's comforting to go back to those seasons.
回到那些季节让人感慨，也让人感到慰藉。

319
00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:38.490
And, you know, I was thinking about which episodes were my favorite, and I know I have my go-tos that I've always liked, like dinner party, things like that.
而且，你知道，我在想哪些集是我最喜欢的，我知道我有一直以来都喜欢的必看集，比如《晚宴》之类的。

320
00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:38.730
Sure, sure.
当然，当然。

321
00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:47.270
But in my rewatch, kind of like you with Mafia, a few that snuck up on me that I'd just forgotten about was, like, the deposition, for example.
但在重温过程中，就像你对《黑手党》那一集的感觉一样，有几集让我感到意外，我都快忘了，比如《取证》那一集。

322
00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:47.990
Love it.
超爱那一集。

323
00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:54.670
Every moment in that deposition when Michael's being cross-examined is just hilarious.
在《取证》里，迈克尔被盘问的每一个瞬间都太搞笑了。

324
00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:57.510
I forgot about sconesy cider.
我都忘了斯康西·赛德了。

325
00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:02.500
Oh, I forget the christening, you know?
噢，我忘了《洗礼》那一集了，你知道吗？

326
00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:03.260
But I do.
但我确实。

327
00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.140
I find myself wanting to go back.
我发现自己想回去重温。

328
00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:08.040
I want to see the first party planning committee meeting.
我想看第一次派对策划委员会会议。

329
00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:08.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

330
00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.440
I want to go back to all of that.
我想回到这一切的起点。

331
00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:19.320
Well, when we talked to Billie Eilish on the podcast, we asked her about rewatching, and I kind of think of her as a rewatch expert because she really has seen it so many times.
嗯，当我们在播客中与比莉·艾利什交谈时，我们问了她关于重温的问题，我觉得她算得上是重温专家，因为她确实看了太多遍了。

332
00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.800
And we asked her, do you ever skip anything?
我们问她，你会跳过什么吗？

333
00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.200
You know, do you have favorite seasons?
你知道，你有最喜欢的季节吗？

334
00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.280
Will you just start with a certain thing?
你会直接从某处开始看吗？

335
00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:27.200
And she said no.
她说不会。

336
00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:35.100
She said she always goes back to the very beginning, and she watches everything, although she did say sometimes she skips Scott's Tots.
她说她总是从头开始，把所有内容都看一遍，不过她确实说过有时会跳过《斯科特的托特们》那一集。

337
00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:36.280
Well, you know.
嗯，你知道的。

338
00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:36.960
That's the only one.
那是唯一一集。

339
00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:37.700
That's okay.
没关系。

340
00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.140
One about the family paper company.
就是关于那家家族造纸公司的。

341
00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:45.000
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

342
00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.640
That they closed down.
他们倒闭了的那家。

343
00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:47.460
They put out a business.
他们让那家公司倒闭了。

344
00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:48.140
Yeah.
是啊。

345
00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:48.440
Yeah.
是啊。

346
00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:49.420
Prince family paper.
普林斯家族造纸公司。

347
00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.240
Prince family paper.
普林斯家族造纸公司。

348
00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.400
That one, I couldn't take it.
那一集，我实在看不下去。

349
00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:51.860
Oh.
噢。

350
00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.500
But, Allison, fantastic question.
不过，艾莉森，这个问题问得太棒了。

351
00:13:55.780 --> 00:14:02.380
It clearly made Jenna and I think a lot about this rewatch and what it's meant to us, and we both want to start back at the beginning.
这显然让珍娜和我对这次重温产生了许多思考，也让我们意识到它对我们的意义，我们俩都想从头开始再看一遍。

352
00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.180
We do.
确实如此。

353
00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.360
But don't worry, we will cover season nine.
但别担心，我们还是会讲到第九季的。

354
00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:05.700
Yes.
是的。

355
00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:06.040
Yes.
没错。

356
00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.180
Not to get ahead of ourselves.
我们不会操之过急。

357
00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:09.520
All right.
好的。

358
00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:13.960
Fast fact number three is a fan question from Curtis G.
第三个冷知识来自粉丝柯蒂斯·G的提问。

359
00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:14.860
in Seattle.
他来自西雅图。

360
00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:25.600
I didn't think there was anything else that we could learn, Angela, about, I don't know, the origins of characters or anything this long into our rewatch.
安吉拉，我本以为重温到这个阶段，关于角色起源之类的东西，我们已经没什么可学的了。

361
00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.160
But Curtis has found something that I didn't know.
但柯蒂斯发现了一些我不知道的事情。

362
00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:28.900
What?
什么？

363
00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.520
Here's what Curtis said.
柯蒂斯是这么说的。

364
00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:35.160
When I was in grad school, one of my professors was named Andy Bernard.
我在读研时，有一位教授叫安迪·伯纳德。

365
00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:41.720
There was a rumor that he and Greg Daniels were friends in college and that Greg named Ed's character after him.
有传言说他和格雷格·丹尼尔斯是大学好友，格雷格是用他的名字给艾德的角色命名的。

366
00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:48.160
Is it true that Andy Bernard on the office is named after Professor Andy Bernard at Dartmouth?
《办公室》里的安迪·伯纳德真的是以达特茅斯学院的安迪·伯纳德教授命名的吗？

367
00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:52.240
I would not be surprised at all because Greg liked to do that.
我一点也不惊讶，因为格雷格就喜欢这么做。

368
00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:53.840
Well, I asked Greg.
嗯，我问过格雷格了。

369
00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:54.720
What'd he say?
他怎么说？

370
00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:57.020
He said, you can tell Curtis G.
他说，你可以告诉柯蒂斯·G。

371
00:14:57.340 --> 00:15:03.120
that it is completely true that Andy Bernard on the office is named after Professor Andy Bernard at Dartmouth.
《办公室》里的安迪·伯纳德确实是以达特茅斯学院的安迪·伯纳德教授命名的，这完全属实。

372
00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:11.800
However, Andy and I and our mutual friend Jim Halpert have been great friends since first grade.
不过，安迪和我以及我们的共同好友吉姆·哈珀特从一年级起就是好朋友了。

373
00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:17.060
So, Greg's two childhood friends are named Jim Halpert and Andy Bernard.
所以，格雷格的两个童年好友分别叫吉姆·哈珀特和安迪·伯纳德。

374
00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:17.600
Yeah.
是啊。

375
00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:19.880
I knew Jim Halpert.
我知道吉姆·哈珀特的事。

376
00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:20.540
Same.
我也是。

377
00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.340
But, oh my gosh.
但是，天哪。

378
00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:27.420
Greg said that it was really fun for him to give the characters his old friends' names.
格雷格说，用老朋友的名字来命名角色让他觉得非常有趣。

379
00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:31.220
He never thought that people would still be asking about it 20 years later.
他从没想过20年后还会有人问起这件事。

380
00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:37.120
Greg also said the real life Andy Bernard is at Dartmouth, which is Cornell's big rival,
格雷格还说，现实生活中的安迪·伯纳德在达特茅斯学院，那是康奈尔大学的死对头，

381
00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:41.480
and that the real Andy Bernard is not much like the character of Andy Bernard.
而且现实中的安迪·伯纳德和剧中的安迪·伯纳德一点也不像。

382
00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:42.840
Well, I should think not.
嗯，我想也是。

383
00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:50.040
He did say he thinks the real Andy Bernard might have had one of those preppy belts with whales on them at one time in the 80s.
他确实说，他觉得现实中的安迪·伯纳德在80年代可能也穿过那种印着鲸鱼图案的学院风腰带。

384
00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.760
But besides that, nothing else.
但除此之外，就没什么相似之处了。

385
00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:55.840
He said the real Andy would never punch his fist through a wall.
他说现实中的安迪绝不会一拳打穿墙壁。

386
00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:02.080
However, Greg said the real life Jim Halpert is very sociable, athletic, and romantic.
不过，格雷格说现实生活中的吉姆·哈珀特非常善于社交、热爱运动且浪漫。

387
00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:02.780
Oh.
哦。

388
00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:08.120
Greg said he was at his wedding, and his marriage was beautiful, and his wife is completely Pam-worthy.
格雷格说他参加过他的婚礼，那场婚礼很美，而且他的妻子完全配得上“帕姆”这个名字。

389
00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:12.860
He has many of the qualities that he wanted the character of Jim to have as well.
他身上具备许多格雷格希望吉姆这个角色也拥有的品质。

390
00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:18.960
Greg said when he met John Krasinski, he reminded him of the real life Jim Halpert.
格雷格说，当他见到约翰·卡拉辛斯基时，他想起了现实生活中的吉姆·哈珀特。

391
00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:22.000
Greg said they're both incredibly admirable men.
格雷格说他们都是非常令人钦佩的人。

392
00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:27.720
Greg said that in real life, Andy Bernard is a renowned economist who studies globalization
格雷格说，在现实生活中，安迪·伯纳德是一位著名的经济学家，专门研究全球化，

393
00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:33.060
and was named by Reuters as one of the world's most influential scientific minds.
并被路透社评为世界上最具影响力的科学头脑之一。

394
00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.420
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

395
00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:40.640
The real life Jim Halpert works in the White House as general counsel to the national cyber director
现实生活中的吉姆·哈珀特在白宫担任国家网络总监的法律总顾问，

396
00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:44.900
trying to write laws to protect people's security and privacy on the internet.
致力于制定法律以保护人们在互联网上的安全和隐私。

397
00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.300
Okay, Greg's friends are really smart.
好吧，格雷格的朋友们真的很聪明。

398
00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:54.040
He said this is why I asked them both if it was okay to share a recent photo of the three of us.
他说这就是为什么我问他们俩是否介意分享一张我们三个人的近照。

399
00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:54.560
Oh.
哦。

400
00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:59.360
And Greg said we can put it in the Office Ladies pod Instagram stories.
格雷格说我们可以把它发到《办公室女士》播客的Instagram快拍里。

401
00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.000
Oh, great.
太棒了。

402
00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.900
Yes, and it's the cutest picture.
没错，而且那张照片可爱极了。

403
00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:06.780
And I'm just imagining these three guys all the way back in first grade.
我脑海里浮现出他们三个从小学一年级开始的样子。

404
00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:07.260
Yeah.
是啊。

405
00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:13.280
There's probably not a photo of that because we just didn't have cameras like we do now, but I love this friendship.
可能没有那时的照片，因为我们当时没有现在这样的相机，但我很喜欢这份友谊。

406
00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:15.740
What a lifelong friendship.
真是终身的友谊。

407
00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:16.320
Yeah.
是啊。

408
00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:17.720
Oh, I love that.
噢，我太喜欢这个了。

409
00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:18.820
Thank you, Greg.
谢谢你，格雷格。

410
00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:21.540
Thank you, Greg, and thank you, Curtis.
谢谢你，格雷格，也谢谢你，柯蒂斯。

411
00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:31.040
Yes, and for all of you Greg Daniels fans out there, you know, season three of Upload is now streaming on Amazon Prime Video.
没错，各位格雷格·丹尼尔斯的粉丝们，你们知道，《上传》第三季现在已经在亚马逊 Prime Video 上线了。

412
00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.720
The trailer is awesome.
预告片太棒了。

413
00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:35.480
We have to put that in our stories, Angela.
安吉拉，我们得把它发到我们的快拍里。

414
00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:39.860
And by the way, if you have not watched Upload, it is so good.
顺便说一下，如果你还没看过《上传》，它真的非常好看。

415
00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:42.840
It has like 93% on Rotten Tomatoes.
它在烂番茄上有 93% 的新鲜度。

416
00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:44.340
You should definitely check it out.
你一定要去看看。

417
00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:47.660
Well, that's all I have for Fast Facts, lady.
好了，这就是我准备的快讯，女士。

418
00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:53.520
Should we get into our last breakdown of an episode from season eight?
我们要开始解析第八季的最后一集了吗？

419
00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:58.160
Let's do it because we have a little bit of old tech that was new tech at the time.
开始吧，因为里面有一些当时算新技术，现在看来是旧科技的东西。

420
00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.020
Oh.
噢。

421
00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.660
Well, we'll take a break and discuss.
那我们休息一下，回来再讨论。

422
00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:16.680
We are back and Oscar is talking directly to a camera on his computer.
我们回来了，奥斯卡正在对着他电脑上的摄像头说话。

423
00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:18.220
He's doing like one of those.
他就像在做那种……

424
00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:19.020
Like a webcam.
就像网络摄像头。

425
00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:23.840
A webcam, like, you know, like one of those confessionals that folks do on YouTube now.
网络摄像头，你知道，就像现在人们在 YouTube 上做的那些访谈视频一样。

426
00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.800
You guys, people were not doing this yet.
伙计们，当时人们还没开始这么做呢。

427
00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:27.020
This was the very beginning.
这还处于非常早期的阶段。

428
00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:33.820
So this whole scene and the way the camera was set up and how Oscar's talking directly to the internet, as I call it.
所以整个这一幕，以及摄像头的设置方式，还有奥斯卡直接对着互联网——我称之为互联网——说话的方式。

429
00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:34.220
Yes.
没错。

430
00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:35.880
That wasn't really happening.
这在当时并不常见。

431
00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.020
And it wasn't featured very much on television.
而且电视节目里也很少出现这种形式。

432
00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:41.060
So this was a little bit of like, you know, new technology.
所以这算是一种比较新的技术。

433
00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:43.560
And of course, now we look at it and we're like, oh my gosh.
当然，现在我们回看这一幕会觉得，天哪。

434
00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:45.300
Yeah, people do it all the time.
是啊，人们现在无时无刻不在做这个。

435
00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:45.940
All the time.
无时无刻。

436
00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:48.180
Well, I asked Steve Burgess, how did we get this shot?
我问了史蒂夫·伯吉斯，我们是怎么拍到这个镜头的？

437
00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:56.940
And he said, Matt Soan just set up one of the cameras on Oscar's desk, moved the computer out of the way, and set the camera there with this sort of special lens.
他说马特·索恩只是把其中一台摄像机架在奥斯卡的桌子上，把电脑移开，然后用那种特殊的镜头对准那里。

438
00:18:57.140 --> 00:19:01.120
And then everybody just walked over and talked into it as if it was a webcam.
然后每个人走过来对着它说话，就像对着网络摄像头一样。

439
00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:02.500
It's very funny.
非常有趣。

440
00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:05.140
You know, Dwight and Phyllis are kind of lurking behind.
你知道，德怀特和菲利斯在后面鬼鬼祟祟的。

441
00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.720
Kelly comes in and touches up her makeup.
凯莉走进来补妆。

442
00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:14.620
Robert then comes in and just starts talking straight to camera, takes over, headbutts Kevin, and then it all falls apart.
罗伯特随后进来，直接对着镜头说话，抢了镜头，还用头撞了凯文，然后一切就乱套了。

443
00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:21.060
So Oscar ultimately tells the youth, you know what, it may not get much better, but it does get a little better.
所以奥斯卡最后告诉年轻人，你知道吗，情况可能不会好转太多，但确实会变好一点点。

444
00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:27.940
Well, this episode opens with a Dwight talking head.
这一集是以德怀特的单人访谈开场的。

445
00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:32.980
And he's explaining that he wanted to give the tenants of the building something nice.
他解释说他想给大楼的租户们提供一些好的服务。

446
00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:37.640
So he has set up a family portrait studio in the break room.
所以他在休息室里搭建了一个全家福摄影棚。

447
00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:43.120
And during this talking head, we're seeing groups of people getting their picture taken.
在这次访谈过程中，我们看到一群群人正在拍照。

448
00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:43.860
Yes.
没错。

449
00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:48.460
I will say for this montage, everyone that's getting their picture taken, there was written dialogue.
我得说，对于这段蒙太奇，每一个拍照的人其实都有写好的台词。

450
00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:49.480
There was?
真的吗？

451
00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:50.940
Yes, that wasn't used.
没错，那段没用上。

452
00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.560
Please tell me more.
请多跟我说说。

453
00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:58.100
Well, Toby and his daughter are doing a dance, and she's like saying, jazz hands, dad, and he can't quite get it.
托比和他的女儿在跳舞，女儿对他说，爸爸，爵士手势，但他总是做不到位。

454
00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:01.300
Stanley and his daughter just have a sweet moment, you know.
斯坦利和他的女儿则有一个温馨的瞬间，你知道的。

455
00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:05.560
And then Creed and his parents, he's like, look, I'm in a parent's sandwich.
还有克里德和他的父母，他说，看，我夹在父母中间了。

456
00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.660
You know, Creed is just being cuckoo pants.
你知道的，克里德就是那么疯疯癫癫的。

457
00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:11.900
And then Meredith and her son just continue to yell at each other.
然后梅雷迪思和她儿子继续互相大吼大叫。

458
00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:12.760
I see.
我明白了。

459
00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:13.100
Yeah.
是啊。

460
00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:15.280
So there was just extra beats of all of it.
所以这些片段都多拍了一些。

461
00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:21.360
Well, if you're wondering who played all the family members, Toby's daughter was played by Delaney Ruth Farrell.
如果你好奇这些家庭成员都是谁演的，托比的女儿是由德莱尼·露丝·法瑞尔饰演的。

462
00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:23.480
She was the daughter of our set dresser.
她是我们的布景师的女儿。

463
00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.340
Stanley's daughter was played by Sarah Rebecca.
斯坦利的女儿由莎拉·丽贝卡饰演。

464
00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.080
Creed's parents were played by Ed Ford Jr.
克里德的父母由小埃德·福特饰演。

465
00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:30.240
and Jackie Beno.
还有杰基·贝诺。

466
00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:34.000
And Meredith's son was played again by Spencer Daniels.
梅雷迪思的儿子依然由斯宾塞·丹尼尔斯饰演。

467
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:43.280
Shout out to our actual NBC set photographer and Kate Flannery's longtime fella, Chris Hastings, for working the Dwight's Family Portrait Studio.
特别感谢我们真正的NBC片场摄影师，也是凯特·弗兰纳里的长期伴侣克里斯·黑斯廷斯，他在德怀特的家庭肖像摄影室里帮忙。

468
00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:44.500
You'll see him in the corner.
你会看到他在角落里。

469
00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:48.440
He's sitting at the desk, kind of logging all the pictures onto the computer.
他坐在桌子旁，负责把照片录入电脑。

470
00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.580
I saw him.
我看到他了。

471
00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:57.320
I also want to share with you guys in the shooting draft, there would have been an establishing shot of the flyer for this free family portrait studio.
我还想和大家分享一下，在拍摄剧本中，原本有一个关于这个免费家庭肖像摄影室传单的定场镜头。

472
00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:58.500
And here's what it said.
上面是这么写的。

473
00:20:58.640 --> 00:20:59.160
Oh, boy.
天哪。

474
00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:09.820
In all caps on the flyer, it says, free family portrait studio, all professional, exclamation point, May 9th, noon to 5 p.m.
传单上用大写字母写着：免费家庭肖像摄影室，全专业水准，感叹号，5月9日，中午12点到下午5点。

475
00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:14.000
in Dunder Mifflin break room, courtesy of building manager Dwight K.
地点在邓德·米夫林休息室，由大楼经理德怀特·K·施鲁特提供。

476
00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:14.520
Schrute.
施鲁特。

477
00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:17.820
All professional, please, guys.
全专业水准，拜托各位。

478
00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:18.800
Keep it professional.
保持专业。

479
00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:22.020
And I have another tidbit to add about this scene.
关于这场戏，我还有个小花絮要补充。

480
00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:22.920
You thought I was done.
你以为我说完了吧。

481
00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:24.000
I've got one, too.
我也有一个。

482
00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.780
It's the scene that keeps on giving.
这真是一场惊喜不断的戏。

483
00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:26.300
Okay.
好吧。

484
00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:27.340
Here's mine.
听我的。

485
00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:34.580
In the shooting draft, the person who was in the very front of the line who would have been first up to get their picture taken was, any guesses?
在拍摄剧本里，排在队伍最前面、第一个去拍照的人是谁，猜猜看？

486
00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:36.960
Oh, this is a good question.
哦，这问题问得好。

487
00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:39.340
Kevin?
凯文？

488
00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:40.580
No.
不是。

489
00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.280
It was Brandon.
是布兰登。

490
00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.780
And this might explain a little bit of that photo at the end.
这或许能解释最后那张照片的一些细节。

491
00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:50.100
Here's how it read, and it's also in deleted scenes.
剧本是这样写的，这段内容也在删减片段里。

492
00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:51.840
Interior break room.
内景，休息室。

493
00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:54.340
Brandon and Val are at the front of the line.
布兰登和瓦尔排在队伍最前面。

494
00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:56.200
Photographer, next up.
摄影师：下一位。

495
00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:59.440
Brandon checks himself in a compact mirror and steps up.
布兰登对着粉饼盒里的镜子整理了一下，走上前去。

496
00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:00.760
Val follows.
瓦尔跟在后面。

497
00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:05.840
Brandon waves her off and says, baby, I need some singles, okay?
布兰登挥手让她走开，说：宝贝，我需要些零钱，好吗？

498
00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:07.640
She says, what?
她说：什么？

499
00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.600
And he goes, I need some singles.
他说：我需要些零钱。

500
00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:11.060
And he shoes her away.
然后把她赶走了。

501
00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:15.980
And then he turns to the photographer and he says, can we clear some of this kid's stuff out of here?
接着他转向摄影师说，能不能把这孩子的东西清理一下？

502
00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:20.280
This is a promotional shot for my restaurant, and I am selling three things.
这是我餐厅的宣传照，我主要卖三样东西。

503
00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:22.360
Food, sex, and laughter.
食物、性和欢笑。

504
00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:28.700
And then he does a series of photos with that kind of in mind.
然后他就带着这种想法拍了一系列照片。

505
00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:32.680
And Val is just sitting on the side just watching him like, what the hell?
瓦尔就坐在旁边看着他，心想，这到底是怎么回事？

506
00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:35.000
He didn't want a picture with his own girlfriend.
他甚至不想和自己的女朋友合影。

507
00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.240
I have a question.
我有个问题。

508
00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:39.140
Is Val wearing her warehouse uniform in this scene?
瓦尔在这一幕里穿的是她的仓库制服吗？

509
00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:39.600
Yes.
是的。

510
00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:40.540
Why?
为什么？

511
00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:47.000
She wants a portrait with her boyfriend, and she's in her, like, work uniform, and he's in regular clothes?
她想和男朋友拍合照，结果她穿着工作服，而他穿着便装？

512
00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:48.520
This is very poor planning.
这计划得太糟糕了。

513
00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:49.440
Well...
嗯……

514
00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:50.620
It bothered me later, too.
后来我也觉得很困扰。

515
00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:51.760
We can talk about it more.
我们可以再多聊聊这个。

516
00:22:52.380 --> 00:22:52.860
Yes.
好的。

517
00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:56.060
It didn't really look like most everyone dressed for this photo.
这看起来确实不像大家为了拍照而精心打扮的样子。

518
00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:58.740
Pam really dressed her kids for this photo.
帕姆确实给她的孩子们精心打扮了。

519
00:22:58.800 --> 00:22:59.660
Pam went all out.
帕姆全力以赴了。

520
00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:01.920
As did Angela, or the senator.
安吉拉和参议员也是。

521
00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:02.620
The senator.
参议员。

522
00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:04.260
Angela had nothing to do with it.
安吉拉对此毫无干系。

523
00:23:04.380 --> 00:23:09.680
But I wanted to share this scene because it just shows you the dynamic of their relationship.
但我之所以想分享这一幕，是因为它展现了他们关系的动态。

524
00:23:09.940 --> 00:23:11.360
He didn't even want a picture with her.
他甚至不想和她合影。

525
00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:13.380
He wanted photos by himself.
他只想自己拍。

526
00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.140
That doesn't feel good.
那感觉真不好。

527
00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:18.360
I wish we had that scene in.
真希望我们保留了那一幕。

528
00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.100
I just want more of Jerry Miner.
我只是想要更多杰瑞·迈纳的戏份。

529
00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:21.900
Oh, he's very funny in it.
哦，他在那里面非常搞笑。

530
00:23:21.980 --> 00:23:22.600
He would have been so good in that.
他要是能演那段肯定很棒。

531
00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:24.500
His poses are hilarious.
他的姿势太滑稽了。

532
00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:27.340
We got a fan catch from Emily J.
我们收到了来自俄亥俄州艾米丽·J的粉丝发现，她说，

533
00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:29.380
in Ohio who said,
克里德带了他的父母来拍照，但在第六季《掩盖》那一集中，克里德说他妈妈去世了。

534
00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:35.540
Creed brings in his parents for a photo, but in season six, the cover-up, Creed says his mom has died.
你知道吗，艾米丽？

535
00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:37.020
You know what, Emily?
你不能相信克里德说的任何话。

536
00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:38.720
You can't trust anything Creed says.
这些人可能根本不是他的父母。

537
00:23:38.840 --> 00:23:40.120
These might not be his parents.
我正想说，他可能在不同地方有多个家庭。

538
00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:44.540
I was going to say, he might have multiple families in different places.
没错。

539
00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:45.120
Yeah.
我觉得这是一个很好的发现，但同时，克里德身上什么事都可能发生。

540
00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:49.300
I think that is a good catch, and at the same time, anything goes with Creed.
是啊。

541
00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:49.620
Yeah.
我想编剧们也把这点记在心里了。

542
00:23:49.880 --> 00:23:51.800
Which I think the writers took to heart.
因为我觉得他的角色设定集有点乱七八糟的。

543
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.700
Because I think his show Bible is a bit squirrely.
完全没有章法。

544
00:23:54.840 --> 00:23:55.580
It's all over the place.
全是各种矛盾。

545
00:23:55.580 --> 00:23:57.200
It's just a bunch of contradictions.
没错。

546
00:23:57.440 --> 00:23:57.600
Yeah.
不过发现得很好。

547
00:23:57.960 --> 00:23:59.100
But very good catch.
德怀特现在走进办公区，宣布照相馆只剩下最后几个小时了。

548
00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:04.800
Dwight now enters the bullpen and announces there's only a few more hours left of the portrait studio.
他建议达里尔带女儿过来，让安吉拉带菲利普过来。

549
00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:08.760
He suggests for Daryl to bring his daughter in, for Angela to bring Phillip.
也许吉姆可以带他那两个可爱的小家伙过来。

550
00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:10.980
Maybe Jim could bring his two cuties.
也许吉姆可以带他那两个可爱的小家伙过来。

551
00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:13.160
And Jim says, you know what?
吉姆说，你知道吗？

552
00:24:13.320 --> 00:24:14.960
I know why Dwight's doing this.
我知道德怀特为什么要这么做。

553
00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:15.440
Yes.
没错。

554
00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:21.500
He has a whole talking head where he describes that he did this elaborate prank where he got Dwight's
他有一整段采访，描述了他策划的这个精心恶作剧，他弄到了德怀特的

555
00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:24.020
suits and made them with tear-away Velcro.
西装，并把它们改成了魔术贴撕拉款。

556
00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:26.820
What is Jim's budget for these pranks?
吉姆做这些恶作剧的预算是多少？

557
00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:29.300
Have you ever had alterations done?
你改过衣服吗？

558
00:24:29.300 --> 00:24:30.460
I'm a short person.
我个子矮。

559
00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:32.160
I have to get everything altered.
我所有衣服都得改。

560
00:24:32.380 --> 00:24:34.180
And it is not cheap.
而且这并不便宜。

561
00:24:34.380 --> 00:24:39.820
Well, you know, Angela, in our fan appreciation mailbag episode, we discussed this scene.
嗯，安吉拉，在我们的粉丝答谢信箱那期节目里，我们讨论过这个场景。

562
00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:40.380
We did.
我们讨论过。

563
00:24:40.380 --> 00:24:42.220
I read a letter from Joe V.
我读了一封来自俄勒冈州乔·V的信，

564
00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:45.840
in Oregon, and he had done an in-depth breakdown of what it
他深入分析了这些年来

565
00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:49.520
costs Jim to prank Dwight over all of these many years.
吉姆捉弄德怀特所花费的成本。

566
00:24:49.520 --> 00:24:53.520
If you haven't listened to that episode and you're interested in really digging deep into
如果你还没听过那期节目，又对深入挖掘

567
00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:55.780
this subject, you can go back and listen to it.
这个话题感兴趣的话，可以回去听听。

568
00:24:56.100 --> 00:24:56.800
Joe V.
俄勒冈州的乔·V

569
00:24:56.980 --> 00:25:02.260
from Oregon, he thinks that this tear-away suit was Jim's second most expensive
认为这套撕拉西装是吉姆第二昂贵的

570
00:25:02.260 --> 00:25:05.220
prank, and he broke down the cost like this.
恶作剧，他是这样拆解成本的。

571
00:25:05.860 --> 00:25:10.220
He had to buy an alternate cheap suit that cost about $200.
他得买一套备用的廉价西装，大约花了200美元。

572
00:25:11.100 --> 00:25:14.160
He had to have a tailor sew Velcro into it.
他得找裁缝把魔术贴缝进去。

573
00:25:14.260 --> 00:25:16.120
He estimates that was $100.
他估计那花了100美元。

574
00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:18.100
Easily $100.
绝对要100美元。

575
00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:18.860
Easily.
肯定的。

576
00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:21.020
And he included a tip for the dry cleaner.
而且他还算上了给干洗店的小费。

577
00:25:21.380 --> 00:25:22.480
That was $10.
那是10美元。

578
00:25:23.400 --> 00:25:26.320
So he estimates this prank cost $310.
所以他估计这个恶作剧花了310美元。

579
00:25:27.300 --> 00:25:27.820
Yeah.
是啊。

580
00:25:28.080 --> 00:25:28.580
I mean...
我是说……

581
00:25:28.580 --> 00:25:29.920
How does Pam feel about that?
帕姆对此怎么看？

582
00:25:30.120 --> 00:25:30.860
I mean, I...
我是说，我……

583
00:25:30.860 --> 00:25:37.400
Is their family so flush with finances that they can afford to spend $310 on this prank?
他们的家庭经济状况真的宽裕到能花310美元在这种恶作剧上吗？

584
00:25:37.720 --> 00:25:38.500
Absolutely not.
绝对没有。

585
00:25:39.040 --> 00:25:39.700
No one.
没人会。

586
00:25:39.780 --> 00:25:42.320
No one wants to spend $300 on a tear-away suit.
没人想花300美元买一套撕拉西装。

587
00:25:42.500 --> 00:25:43.320
Like, what are you doing?
这到底是在干什么？

588
00:25:43.640 --> 00:25:43.860
Yeah.
没错。

589
00:25:44.220 --> 00:25:45.260
I will say this.
我得说一句。

590
00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:45.740
What?
什么？

591
00:25:45.920 --> 00:25:47.440
Maybe we'll get mail about it.
也许我们会收到关于这个的来信。

592
00:25:47.680 --> 00:25:48.220
What is it?
是什么？

593
00:25:48.260 --> 00:25:49.100
But I'm just going to say it.
但我还是要说出来。

594
00:25:49.180 --> 00:25:49.680
What is it?
是什么？

595
00:25:50.020 --> 00:25:53.240
I think Jim's pranks are Roy's jet skis.
我觉得吉姆的恶作剧就像罗伊的喷气滑雪板一样。

596
00:25:53.840 --> 00:25:54.240
Hmm.
嗯。

597
00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:55.540
Oh, boy.
天哪。

598
00:25:55.760 --> 00:25:56.100
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

599
00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:58.240
Angela, that is a strong statement.
安吉拉，这评价可真够狠的。

600
00:25:58.240 --> 00:25:59.500
It's a strong statement.
这评价确实很重。

601
00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:02.920
But if you add up everything Jim spends on pranks, what...
但如果你把吉姆花在恶作剧上的所有钱加起来，那……

602
00:26:02.920 --> 00:26:05.060
Could that be a vacation for their family?
那够他们一家去度假吗？

603
00:26:05.320 --> 00:26:06.520
Could they go to Disneyland?
他们能去迪士尼乐园吗？

604
00:26:07.060 --> 00:26:11.380
Could they maybe, you know, splurge and buy that new sofa they've been wanting?
他们或许能，你知道的，挥霍一下，买下他们一直想要的那张新沙发吗？

605
00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:12.180
No.
不能。

606
00:26:12.460 --> 00:26:13.820
They bought a tear-away suit.
他们买了一套撕拉式西装。

607
00:26:14.180 --> 00:26:15.300
Ooh, Angela.
噢，安吉拉。

608
00:26:15.700 --> 00:26:16.440
Oh, boy.
天哪。

609
00:26:17.420 --> 00:26:19.240
I had not ever thought of it.
我之前从没想过这一点。

610
00:26:19.360 --> 00:26:21.880
Here's my yes and to that theory.
对于这个理论，我完全赞同并补充一点。

611
00:26:22.640 --> 00:26:26.080
Do you think Jim checked in with Pam before doing this?
你觉得吉姆在做这件事之前跟帕姆商量过吗？

612
00:26:26.240 --> 00:26:28.180
Did he say, hey, babe, I have a hilarious idea.
他有没有说，嘿，宝贝，我有个超搞笑的点子。

613
00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:29.260
What if?
如果我……

614
00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:31.340
I do a tear-away suit.
穿一套撕拉式西装怎么样？

615
00:26:31.740 --> 00:26:34.360
And then did she say, how much is that going to cost?
然后她有没有说，那要花多少钱？

616
00:26:34.500 --> 00:26:36.800
And he said, I don't know, maybe $300, $310.
他说，我不知道，大概300、310美元吧。

617
00:26:37.020 --> 00:26:37.600
But remember...
但你要记住……

618
00:26:37.600 --> 00:26:38.740
And she said, that's hilarious.
然后她说，那太搞笑了。

619
00:26:38.740 --> 00:26:39.440
We should do it.
我们应该这么做。

620
00:26:39.500 --> 00:26:41.000
Do you think he consulted her?
你觉得他征求过她的意见吗？

621
00:26:41.240 --> 00:26:43.580
He bought a whole house without talking to her.
他连买房子都没跟她商量过。

622
00:26:44.020 --> 00:26:45.440
Well, now we're going there.
好吧，现在我们开始讨论这个了。

623
00:26:45.580 --> 00:26:49.860
Well, I'm just saying, people come for Pam all the time.
我只是说，大家总是针对帕姆。

624
00:26:49.860 --> 00:26:55.500
But we don't discuss exactly what you said, which is that there's no trips to Disneyland
但我们没讨论你刚才说的那点，也就是因为我们要捉弄同事，

625
00:26:55.500 --> 00:27:00.400
because we're pranking our coworker and not talking to our wife about it firSt.
而且没先跟妻子商量，所以就没法去迪士尼乐园了。

626
00:27:00.400 --> 00:27:01.540
Yeah.
没错。

627
00:27:01.940 --> 00:27:03.340
We're on to something here.
我们发现了一些端倪。

628
00:27:03.500 --> 00:27:09.720
I think that there is a pattern of Jim spending the couple's money without consulting Pam.
我觉得吉姆确实有不跟帕姆商量就花夫妻共同财产的习惯。

629
00:27:10.140 --> 00:27:12.280
We're going to see it coming up again.
我们接下来还会看到这种情况。

630
00:27:12.780 --> 00:27:16.920
I think these pranks are the jet skis.
我觉得这些恶作剧就像是摩托艇。

631
