00:46:06.560 --> 00:46:09.680
It's literally exactly the same duck I went back and looked.
说到鸭子，大家还记得我们请克莱尔来做客时，聊到她从片场拿走了那只发声鸭子吗？

1129
00:46:09.920 --> 00:46:17.420
Speaking of ducks, you guys, you'll remember when we had Claire on, how we talked that she took from set the quacking duck.
不是这一幕里那只毛绒鸭子，Christopher。

1130
00:46:17.600 --> 00:46:20.280
Not the stuffed animal duck that's in this scene, Christopher.
是不同的鸭子。

1131
00:46:20.540 --> 00:46:21.140
Different duck.
就是菲利斯办公桌旁文件柜上的那只小鸭子。

1132
00:46:21.140 --> 00:46:25.100
The little duck that sat by the file cabinet by Phyllis's desk.
它总是在拍摄过程中突然叫起来，毁掉了一次又一次的拍摄。

1133
00:46:25.280 --> 00:46:28.280
That would go off during takes and ruin take after take.
没错。

1134
00:46:28.420 --> 00:46:28.680
Yes.
前几天早上，克莱尔给我发了这个。

1135
00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:31.100
Well, Claire sent this to me the other morning.
一大早，我来读读她说了什么。

1136
00:46:31.320 --> 00:46:34.440
First thing in the morning, I'm going to read what she said.
她说，嘿，安吉，这个小家伙跟你问好。

1137
00:46:34.620 --> 00:46:37.620
She goes, Hey, Ange, good morning from this little guy.
然后她拍了一段自己按压那只鸭子的视频。

1138
00:46:37.620 --> 00:46:41.040
And then she took a video of herself hitting the duck.
伙计们，这就是那只毁掉了一次又一次拍摄的鸭子。

1139
00:46:41.220 --> 00:46:44.660
This is the duck, guys, that would ruin take after take.
它听起来是这样的。

1140
00:46:44.780 --> 00:46:45.920
This is what it sounded like.
我凭记忆就能模仿出来。

1141
00:46:55.130 --> 00:46:56.770
I could do it from memory.
嘎，嘎，嘎，嘎，嘎，嘎。

1142
00:46:57.190 --> 00:46:59.030
Quack, quack, quack, quack, quack, quack.
不对，它有一种独特的节奏。

1143
00:46:59.030 --> 00:47:00.710
No, it has a little cadence.
它有一种独特的节奏，嘎，嘎，嘎。

1144
00:47:00.910 --> 00:47:02.230
It has a little cadence, quack, quack, quack.
人们常说，有些声音能让你瞬间回到第一次听到它们的时候，这声音绝对做到了。

1145
00:47:02.410 --> 00:47:07.770
They say some sounds take you right back to where you were the moment you first heard them, and that definitely does.
我会把它发到快拍里，这样你们就能看到那只著名的发声鸭子了。

1146
00:47:07.770 --> 00:47:11.270
I'm going to put that in stories so you can see the famous quacking duck.
你应该发。

1147
00:47:11.450 --> 00:47:12.050
You should.
参议员带着安吉拉的宝宝菲利普到了。

1148
00:47:12.570 --> 00:47:15.990
The senator arrives with Angela's baby, Philip.
安吉拉当时的样子是，不，不，不，不，不。

1149
00:47:16.770 --> 00:47:18.010
Angela's like, No, no, no, no, no.
你来这儿干什么？

1150
00:47:18.050 --> 00:47:18.790
What are you doing here?
你来这儿干什么？

1151
00:47:18.790 --> 00:47:24.090
Yes, baby Philip Lipton, also played by twin girls, Allie and Suzanne Hartman.
没错，宝贝菲利普·利普顿也是由双胞胎女孩艾莉和苏珊·哈特曼饰演的。

1152
00:47:24.850 --> 00:47:28.290
Well, Dwight is going to welcome Angela and the senator to the photo studio.
德怀特要在照相馆迎接安吉拉和参议员。

1153
00:47:28.590 --> 00:47:30.470
Angela will not let Dwight hold Philip.
安吉拉不让德怀特抱菲利普。

1154
00:47:30.650 --> 00:47:32.730
Dwight keeps trying to get near Philip.
德怀特一直试图靠近菲利普。

1155
00:47:33.330 --> 00:47:38.950
Angela has a talking head where she says she thinks Dwight's doing this whole thing to get a DNA sample to prove he's the father,
安吉拉在采访中说，她认为德怀特做这一切是为了获取DNA样本，以证明他是孩子的父亲，

1156
00:47:39.110 --> 00:47:43.650
which is impossible because the senator is the only man she's ever been with.
但这根本不可能，因为参议员是她唯一的男人。

1157
00:47:43.790 --> 00:47:44.950
I have a question for you.
我有个问题想问你。

1158
00:47:45.150 --> 00:47:45.730
What is it?
什么问题？

1159
00:47:45.730 --> 00:47:46.710
What's up with my hair?
我的头发是怎么回事？

1160
00:47:46.890 --> 00:47:48.410
What is up with your hair?
你的头发怎么了？

1161
00:47:48.610 --> 00:47:50.970
It looked like I had just been in a wind tunnel.
看起来就像我刚从风洞里出来一样。

1162
00:47:51.170 --> 00:47:52.630
What is up with your hair?
你的头发到底怎么了？

1163
00:47:52.830 --> 00:47:56.690
And then immediately when I go to the family portrait studio, it's totally normal.
然后当我立刻去拍全家福时，它又完全正常了。

1164
00:47:56.890 --> 00:47:58.270
What happened to my hair?
我的头发发生了什么？

1165
00:47:58.670 --> 00:48:00.650
I wondered if there was a deleted scene.
我当时就在想是不是有删减片段。

1166
00:48:00.910 --> 00:48:03.390
Are you ripping your hair out in frustration?
你是气得在揪自己的头发吗？

1167
00:48:03.410 --> 00:48:04.050
It's odd.
这很奇怪。

1168
00:48:04.250 --> 00:48:05.010
It's very odd.
非常奇怪。

1169
00:48:05.210 --> 00:48:06.690
I went to the shooting draft.
我查了拍摄剧本。

1170
00:48:06.890 --> 00:48:08.170
I went to the candy bag.
我查了花絮资料。

1171
00:48:08.350 --> 00:48:09.630
I watched deleted scenes.
我看了删减片段。

1172
00:48:09.890 --> 00:48:14.890
There is no mention of Angela looking disheveled, her hair a mess.
里面根本没提到安吉拉看起来衣衫不整、头发凌乱。

1173
00:48:14.890 --> 00:48:19.870
I was trying to think if maybe, you know, we would do a series of talking heads in a row.
我当时在想，也许我们是不是连续拍了一组采访镜头。

1174
00:48:20.130 --> 00:48:23.850
I was trying to imagine what had happened, why my hair would look like that.
我试图想象发生了什么，为什么我的头发会变成那样。

1175
00:48:23.930 --> 00:48:28.230
And all I could think of is that I was holding a real baby.
我唯一能想到的是，当时我抱着一个真正的婴儿。

1176
00:48:28.230 --> 00:48:33.590
If maybe the baby had touched my hair somehow or I have a little burp cloth.
也许是婴儿碰到了我的头发，或者我拿着一块拍嗝布。

1177
00:48:33.770 --> 00:48:36.790
Maybe I had tried to put it on the other side and tossed my hair.
也许我当时想把它别到另一边，所以拨弄了头发。

1178
00:48:37.190 --> 00:48:37.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1179
00:48:37.630 --> 00:48:38.950
I noticed it as well.
我也注意到了。

1180
00:48:39.490 --> 00:48:44.690
Well, speaking of messy hair, Dwight wants to try and comb baby Phillip's hair, but Angela
说到凌乱的头发，德怀特想给小菲利普梳头，但安吉拉

1181
00:48:44.690 --> 00:48:45.770
swats him away.
把他拍开了。

1182
00:48:46.190 --> 00:48:47.650
These scenes were so fun.
这些场景太有趣了。

1183
00:48:47.770 --> 00:48:49.510
They were so funny, Angela.
它们太搞笑了，安吉拉。

1184
00:48:49.690 --> 00:48:51.130
Can we keep going with them?
我们能继续聊这些吗？

1185
00:48:51.350 --> 00:48:56.710
Because Dwight is also going to suggest he trim Phillip's toenails.
因为德怀特后来还要提议给菲利普剪脚趾甲。

1186
00:48:56.790 --> 00:48:57.210
I know.
我知道。

1187
00:48:57.550 --> 00:49:03.250
Every time Rain is Dwight came at us and I got to swat him away, it was so fun.
每次雷恩饰演的德怀特凑过来，我不得不把他拍开时，都觉得特别好玩。

1188
00:49:03.250 --> 00:49:07.270
And he's going to try to collect excess dry skin.
而且他还要试图收集多余的死皮。

1189
00:49:07.610 --> 00:49:08.270
Oh, I know.
噢，我知道。

1190
00:49:08.430 --> 00:49:14.010
Could you imagine if like a photographer at a baby studio was like fussing over your baby
你能想象如果婴儿照相馆的摄影师像这样

1191
00:49:14.010 --> 00:49:14.630
like this?
对你的孩子大惊小怪吗？

1192
00:49:14.730 --> 00:49:17.810
Also, isn't the senator like, what are you doing, Dwight?
还有，参议员难道不会觉得，德怀特，你在干什么？

1193
00:49:18.310 --> 00:49:20.110
Like the senator is so checked out.
参议员完全不在状态。

1194
00:49:20.290 --> 00:49:21.490
He's so unaware.
他什么都不知道。

1195
00:49:21.830 --> 00:49:22.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1196
00:49:22.570 --> 00:49:23.670
Oh, you know what?
噢，你知道吗？

1197
00:49:23.670 --> 00:49:29.910
I should give a shout out to Julie Dove, who played our fake photographer in all of these
我得向朱莉·多夫致敬，她在所有这些场景中

1198
00:49:29.910 --> 00:49:30.210
scenes.
饰演了我们的假摄影师。

1199
00:49:30.210 --> 00:49:31.170
She was very good.
她演得非常好。

1200
00:49:31.170 --> 00:49:35.470
Well, little baby Phillip Lipton is going to make the poopskies.
好吧，小宝贝菲利普·利普顿要拉臭臭了。

1201
00:49:35.770 --> 00:49:35.990
Yep.
没错。

1202
00:49:36.290 --> 00:49:39.110
The senator takes him out to change his diaper.
参议员带他出去换尿布了。

1203
00:49:39.310 --> 00:49:39.950
Very helpful.
真贴心。

1204
00:49:40.410 --> 00:49:42.090
Refreshing to see that.
看到这一幕真让人耳目一新。

1205
00:49:42.370 --> 00:49:46.850
And Dwight is then going to emerge from the bathroom with a diaper.
然后德怀特会带着尿布从洗手间出来。

1206
00:49:47.130 --> 00:49:47.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1207
00:49:47.850 --> 00:49:51.310
Angela notices this and screams for him and runs after him.
安吉拉注意到了，对他尖叫并追了上去。

1208
00:49:51.690 --> 00:49:55.510
Where did Senator Lipton change the diaper in the men's restroom?
利普顿参议员是在男厕所哪里换的尿布？

1209
00:49:55.750 --> 00:49:56.790
I don't know.
我不知道。

1210
00:49:56.930 --> 00:49:58.990
Because I don't think there's a changing table in there.
因为我觉得那里面根本没有尿布台。

1211
00:49:59.090 --> 00:50:00.190
Well, there's definitely not.
嗯，确实没有。

1212
00:50:00.190 --> 00:50:03.670
I don't think there's a changing table in the women's restroom at Dunder Mifflin.
我觉得邓德·米夫林的女厕所里也没有尿布台。

1213
00:50:03.770 --> 00:50:08.150
Maybe he just laid him down like on the carpet near Kelly's desk.
也许他只是把他放在凯利办公桌旁的地毯上换的。

1214
00:50:08.430 --> 00:50:10.750
And then he threw it away all the way in the bathroom.
然后他把尿布扔到了洗手间里。

1215
00:50:10.790 --> 00:50:11.370
I don't know.
我不知道。

1216
00:50:11.510 --> 00:50:13.210
These are logistics I can't get into.
这些后勤细节我可搞不清楚。

1217
00:50:13.430 --> 00:50:18.490
There's also something that I noticed because we rarely have this angle where we're in the
我还注意到一件事，因为我们很少有这种角度，就是我们像这样在厨房里，

1218
00:50:18.490 --> 00:50:22.850
kitchen like this and we shoot kind of into the bullpen in this way.
然后从这个角度拍摄办公区。

1219
00:50:23.050 --> 00:50:23.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1220
00:50:23.210 --> 00:50:27.930
And I noticed that at 10 minutes and 30 seconds, Leslie has a heater under his desk.
我注意到在10分30秒的时候，莱斯利桌子底下有个加热器。

1221
00:50:27.970 --> 00:50:29.110
Oh, I saw that too.
哦，我也看到了。

1222
00:50:29.130 --> 00:50:30.890
And I thought Leslie got cold.
我还以为是莱斯利冷了。

1223
00:50:30.890 --> 00:50:31.790
I never knew that.
我以前从没注意过。

1224
00:50:31.790 --> 00:50:33.250
I knew we had heaters.
我知道我们有加热器。

1225
00:50:33.430 --> 00:50:34.170
I know.
我知道。

1226
00:50:34.470 --> 00:50:36.770
I thought only the ladies had heaters.
我以为只有女士才有加热器。

1227
00:50:36.890 --> 00:50:38.950
Because the men would wear full suits.
因为男士们都穿着全套西装。

1228
00:50:39.150 --> 00:50:39.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1229
00:50:39.410 --> 00:50:40.350
They were always hot.
他们总是很热。

1230
00:50:40.530 --> 00:50:41.350
They were warm.
他们很暖和。

1231
00:50:41.410 --> 00:50:45.070
But we would have our tights and our skirts and everything.
但我们得穿连裤袜和裙子之类的。

1232
00:50:45.710 --> 00:50:46.770
I didn't know this.
我以前不知道这个。

1233
00:50:46.910 --> 00:50:47.810
All these years.
这么多年了。

1234
00:50:48.090 --> 00:50:49.110
I didn't know it either.
我也不知道。

1235
00:50:49.310 --> 00:50:50.090
Learn something new.
又学到新东西了。

1236
00:50:50.430 --> 00:50:54.170
Well, we should probably go back and discuss Andy.
好吧，我们大概该回去讨论安迪了。

1237
00:50:54.610 --> 00:50:56.870
We should because there's a lot going on.
是该讨论了，因为发生了很多事。

1238
00:50:57.030 --> 00:50:58.790
He's going to gargle some whiskey.
他要用威士忌漱口。

1239
00:50:58.790 --> 00:51:00.050
He's going to choke on it.
他会被呛到的。

1240
00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:05.430
He then brings out soup for Nelly but then spills it all over himself and then tries to
然后他给奈莉端来了汤，结果洒了自己一身，接着试图

1241
00:51:05.430 --> 00:51:06.850
eat it off of his clothes.
从衣服上把汤吃掉。

1242
00:51:07.270 --> 00:51:07.910
Off his arm.
从胳膊上吃。

1243
00:51:08.550 --> 00:51:10.090
Erin's going to pull Andy aside.
艾琳要把安迪拉到一边。

1244
00:51:10.290 --> 00:51:13.650
She's going to say, hey, the payoff for this is going to be delicious.
她会说，嘿，这事儿的回报会很棒的。

1245
00:51:14.430 --> 00:51:17.330
But some of these images are going to be hard to shake, Andy.
但有些画面会让你难以忘怀，安迪。

1246
00:51:17.750 --> 00:51:17.950
You know?
你知道吗？

1247
00:51:18.050 --> 00:51:19.090
So calibrate.
所以调整一下吧。

1248
00:51:19.650 --> 00:51:25.490
Erin is having such a smart, practical, sober moment here.
艾琳在这里表现得非常聪明、务实且清醒。

1249
00:51:26.110 --> 00:51:27.270
Yes, she is.
没错，确实如此。

1250
00:51:27.290 --> 00:51:30.510
But she also co-signed on Drunken Chimney Sweep.
但她也认可了那个“醉酒扫烟囱工”的表演。

1251
00:51:30.730 --> 00:51:31.550
She did.
她确实这么做了。

1252
00:51:32.070 --> 00:51:35.510
But I appreciate her pumping the brakes on this.
但我很感激她在这件事上踩了刹车。

1253
00:51:36.430 --> 00:51:40.570
Meanwhile, Daryl is going to bring Hiday and Glenn down to the warehouse.
与此同时，达里尔打算带海迪和格伦去仓库。

1254
00:51:40.570 --> 00:51:42.310
He's given them their jobs back.
他让他们复职了。

1255
00:51:42.310 --> 00:51:45.490
He's going to reacquaint them with the goings-on.
他打算让他们重新熟悉一下那里的工作情况。

1256
00:51:45.750 --> 00:51:46.350
Yes.
是的。

1257
00:51:46.550 --> 00:51:52.730
He tells them about Val and just really gushes on her as the foreman of the warehouse.
他向他们提到了瓦尔，并对这位仓库工头赞不绝口。

1258
00:51:53.630 --> 00:51:57.290
Brandon hears this and accuses Daryl of hitting on Val.
布兰登听到了，指责达里尔在打瓦尔的主意。

1259
00:51:57.490 --> 00:51:59.930
And Daryl goes, yeah, I am.
达里尔回答说，没错，我就是在打她主意。

1260
00:52:00.030 --> 00:52:01.510
Let's just get that out there.
咱们就把话挑明了吧。

1261
00:52:01.510 --> 00:52:03.230
So we're all on the same page.
这样我们就达成共识了。

1262
00:52:03.390 --> 00:52:08.870
And then Brandon starts personally attacking Daryl.
然后布兰登开始对达里尔进行人身攻击。

1263
00:52:09.690 --> 00:52:13.250
And oh, does Daryl do the right thing here?
噢，达里尔在这里做得对吗？

1264
00:52:13.730 --> 00:52:16.010
He just is like, good luck.
他只是说，祝你好运。

1265
00:52:16.190 --> 00:52:16.450
Yeah.
没错。

1266
00:52:16.870 --> 00:52:18.230
Doesn't insult him back.
没有回敬侮辱。

1267
00:52:18.390 --> 00:52:23.070
Just lets that bad behavior just sit there with a giant spotlight on it.
只是任由那种恶劣的行为暴露在聚光灯下。

1268
00:52:23.210 --> 00:52:24.390
Just wonderful restraint.
真是极好的克制力。

1269
00:52:24.710 --> 00:52:25.330
Absolutely.
绝对是。

1270
00:52:25.330 --> 00:52:31.130
And now we know that there was already a moment in this day where Brandon has pushed Val aside,
现在我们知道，今天早些时候布兰登就已经把瓦尔推到一边，

1271
00:52:31.490 --> 00:52:38.210
taken photos by himself, and now he's being shitty to Daryl when Daryl was just giving
自己拍了照片，而现在当达里尔只是在称赞瓦尔的工作时，

1272
00:52:38.210 --> 00:52:40.450
her compliments on her job.
他又对达里尔态度恶劣。

1273
00:52:40.450 --> 00:52:41.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1274
00:52:41.210 --> 00:52:43.270
So you see this building for Val.
所以你能看出瓦尔所受的委屈。

1275
00:52:43.870 --> 00:52:50.430
Meanwhile, upstairs, some of the folks in the office are going to take Andy into the conference
与此同时，楼上办公室里的一些人打算把安迪带进会议室，

1276
00:52:50.430 --> 00:52:53.490
room and have a kind of intervention.
对他进行某种干预。

1277
00:52:54.030 --> 00:52:54.590
Yeah.
没错。

1278
00:52:54.850 --> 00:52:58.130
And I say some of the people because there are people missing.
我说“一些人”是因为有些人不在场。

1279
00:52:58.950 --> 00:53:02.010
And it really begs the question, where is Robert?
这确实引出了一个问题：罗伯特在哪儿？

1280
00:53:03.030 --> 00:53:07.430
Robert, he usually works in the conference room, but he's not in there now.
罗伯特平时都在会议室办公，但他现在不在那儿。

1281
00:53:07.690 --> 00:53:11.610
And he can't be in the break room because there is a portrait studio happening.
他不可能在休息室，因为那里正在进行肖像摄影。

1282
00:53:11.910 --> 00:53:13.450
He's not in the bullpen.
他也不在办公区。

1283
00:53:13.690 --> 00:53:16.670
He's running errands for his threesome later that evening.
他正在为那天晚上他的三人行跑腿。

1284
00:53:16.890 --> 00:53:17.110
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1285
00:53:17.370 --> 00:53:23.030
He's buying all the things he's going to need for his night of hosting.
他正在采购他当晚做东所需的一切物品。

1286
00:53:23.490 --> 00:53:23.730
Right.
对。

1287
00:53:24.430 --> 00:53:25.370
We might be right.
我们可能是对的。

1288
00:53:25.810 --> 00:53:27.570
Dwight and Angela are in a car chase.
德怀特和安吉拉正在进行一场追车戏。

1289
00:53:27.570 --> 00:53:28.650
We'll get to that.
我们待会儿再说这个。

1290
00:53:28.810 --> 00:53:29.730
Yes, they're gone.
是的，他们不在。

1291
00:53:29.730 --> 00:53:34.210
But I don't think that Meredith went into the conference room.
但我觉得梅雷迪思没去会议室。

1292
00:53:34.510 --> 00:53:36.390
Well, I don't think she'd want to attend one.
嗯，我觉得她也不会想参加那种会议。

1293
00:53:36.650 --> 00:53:37.850
You might be right.
你可能是对的。

1294
00:53:38.390 --> 00:53:44.030
There's a very fun moment where there's a knock at the door and Andy thinks that it must be
有个非常有趣的时刻，有人敲门，安迪以为一定是

1295
00:53:44.030 --> 00:53:44.870
David Wallace.
大卫·华莱士。

1296
00:53:45.310 --> 00:53:45.870
Yes.
是的。

1297
00:53:46.030 --> 00:53:46.290
It is.
确实是他。

1298
00:53:46.490 --> 00:53:48.690
He's ready for his delicious moment.
他准备好迎接他那美妙的时刻了。

1299
00:53:48.890 --> 00:53:49.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1300
00:53:49.450 --> 00:53:50.330
It's Gabe.
是盖博。

1301
00:53:50.530 --> 00:53:53.810
He's wearing a tiny birthday hat and carrying a tiny cupcake.
他戴着一顶小小的生日帽，手里拿着一个小纸杯蛋糕。

1302
00:53:54.010 --> 00:53:56.190
And he says, happy birthday to Gabe.
他说，祝盖博生日快乐。

1303
00:53:56.590 --> 00:53:58.610
Nellie says, get out of here, skeleton man.
奈莉说，走开，骷髅人。

1304
00:53:59.310 --> 00:54:01.130
But now Andy's phone is going to ring.
但现在安迪的手机要响了。

1305
00:54:01.310 --> 00:54:02.950
He's going to step out to take the call.
他会走出去接这个电话。

1306
00:54:03.110 --> 00:54:04.050
And it's not good news.
而且那不是什么好消息。

1307
00:54:04.190 --> 00:54:05.550
David Wallace is stuck in traffic.
大卫·华莱士堵在路上了。

1308
00:54:05.730 --> 00:54:07.450
He thinks maybe he'll come a different day.
他觉得也许他会改天再来。

1309
00:54:07.830 --> 00:54:09.410
Andy's like, you have to come today.
安迪说，你今天必须得来。

1310
00:54:09.670 --> 00:54:09.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1311
00:54:10.090 --> 00:54:12.210
I am fully committed to this bit.
我完全投入到这个桥段里了。

1312
00:54:12.410 --> 00:54:13.490
You've got to come today.
你今天一定要来。

1313
00:54:14.650 --> 00:54:18.210
Then there was a moment in this group scene that really cracked me up.
然后在这个群戏片段里，有一个瞬间真的把我逗乐了。

1314
00:54:18.210 --> 00:54:23.710
It's when Andy says he's been talking to David Wallace all the time.
就是安迪说他一直都在和大卫·华莱士通话的时候。

1315
00:54:23.730 --> 00:54:24.770
And they're like, really?
他们就说，真的吗？

1316
00:54:25.230 --> 00:54:25.890
Like, really?
就是说，真的吗？

1317
00:54:26.270 --> 00:54:26.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1318
00:54:26.810 --> 00:54:28.310
But Aaron's like, it's true.
但亚伦说，是真的。

1319
00:54:28.530 --> 00:54:28.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1320
00:54:28.770 --> 00:54:29.770
He's always talking to him.
他确实一直在和他通话。

1321
00:54:29.850 --> 00:54:31.510
And they're like, have you seen David Wallace?
然后他们就问，你见过大卫·华莱士吗？

1322
00:54:31.650 --> 00:54:32.850
And Aaron's like, oh, no.
亚伦就说，哦，没有。

1323
00:54:33.610 --> 00:54:34.490
I haven't.
我没见过。

1324
00:54:34.790 --> 00:54:38.670
And then when Toby says, do you see David Wallace right now?
然后当托比问，你现在能看到大卫·华莱士吗？

1325
00:54:38.810 --> 00:54:39.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1326
00:54:39.410 --> 00:54:40.670
Do you see him in the room?
你能在这个房间里看到他吗？

1327
00:54:40.790 --> 00:54:40.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1328
00:54:40.990 --> 00:54:43.390
And he also keeps saying his name.
而且他还不时地叫他的名字。

1329
00:54:43.730 --> 00:54:44.730
Hey, Andy.
嘿，安迪。

1330
00:54:45.310 --> 00:54:45.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1331
00:54:45.830 --> 00:54:47.530
We're worried about you, Andy.
我们很担心你，安迪。

1332
00:54:47.950 --> 00:54:49.830
He's like, stop saying my name.
他就说，别再叫我的名字了。

1333
00:54:49.970 --> 00:54:51.870
I thought all of that was really good writing.
我觉得所有这些剧本写得都非常好。

1334
00:54:52.110 --> 00:54:52.570
I did, too.
我也是这么觉得。

1335
00:54:53.030 --> 00:54:58.110
Well, while all of that is happening up in the bullpen, there is a full-on car chase happening.
好吧，就在办公区发生这一切的同时，外面正在上演一场激烈的汽车追逐战。

1336
00:54:58.650 --> 00:55:00.670
Dwight has peeled out of the parking lot.
德怀特已经从停车场飞驰而去了。

1337
00:55:00.810 --> 00:55:02.530
Angela is in hot pursuit.
安吉拉紧追不舍。

1338
00:55:03.370 --> 00:55:09.950
We got a fan question from Rider N in Idaho who said, what are the logistics of filming a car chase like this?
我们收到了来自爱达荷州Rider N的一位粉丝提问，他说，拍摄这样一场汽车追逐战的后勤工作是怎样的？

1339
00:55:09.950 --> 00:55:11.530
And how did you get the second car?
你们是怎么弄到第二辆车的？

1340
00:55:11.850 --> 00:55:15.150
Well, I asked Steve Burgess about this, Rider.
嗯，我问过史蒂夫·伯吉斯这个问题，Rider。

1341
00:55:16.190 --> 00:55:22.910
Basically, we did an elaborate breakdown of the shots that we needed for all of the elements of this car chase.
基本上，我们对这场汽车追逐战所需的所有镜头元素进行了详尽的拆解。

1342
00:55:22.930 --> 00:55:24.630
We had to close streets.
我们必须封闭街道。

1343
00:55:24.970 --> 00:55:26.870
We had lots of safety meetings.
我们开了许多安全会议。

1344
00:55:27.010 --> 00:55:29.250
We had our stunt coordinator, A.I.
我们的特技协调员A.I.

1345
00:55:29.390 --> 00:55:32.570
Jones, on set, had to talk everyone through each sequence.
琼斯在片场，必须向每个人讲解每一个动作序列。

1346
00:55:32.810 --> 00:55:33.170
Yep.
没错。

1347
00:55:33.450 --> 00:55:39.710
Because these sequences involved not only the cars, but also all of the insert cars with cameras on them.
因为这些序列不仅涉及汽车，还涉及所有安装了摄像机的插入式拍摄车。

1348
00:55:39.710 --> 00:55:40.230
That's right.
说得对。

1349
00:55:40.450 --> 00:55:43.950
The LAPD has to come out and deal with all the traffic.
洛杉矶警察局必须出面处理所有的交通问题。

1350
00:55:43.950 --> 00:55:44.830
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

1351
00:55:45.190 --> 00:55:48.110
So Steve said this was a big one for us.
史蒂夫说这对我们来说很重要。

1352
00:55:48.230 --> 00:55:48.690
It was.
确实如此。

1353
00:55:48.790 --> 00:55:51.630
And the car chase had more than one location.
而且那场追车戏不止一个拍摄地点。

1354
00:55:52.530 --> 00:55:54.290
There was a lot more to it.
内容远不止这些。

1355
00:55:54.370 --> 00:55:55.650
It's in deleted scenes.
都在删减片段里。

1356
00:55:55.670 --> 00:56:00.250
And in the shooting draft, I want to share with you guys two things we filmed that you don't see.
在拍摄剧本里，我想和大家分享两个我们拍了但你们没看到的片段。

1357
00:56:00.470 --> 00:56:05.590
First of all, when Angela is following Dwight, he pulls over on the side of the road.
首先，当安吉拉跟着德怀特时，他在路边停了车。

1358
00:56:05.590 --> 00:56:09.910
She pulls over behind him, and he throws a diaper out the car window.
她在他后面停下，他从车窗扔出一个尿布。

1359
00:56:10.190 --> 00:56:16.050
In the shooting draft, it said, after Dwight throws the diaper out the window, Angela stops her car, runs after it.
拍摄剧本里写着，德怀特把尿布扔出窗外后，安吉拉停下车，跑过去捡。

1360
00:56:16.150 --> 00:56:18.390
So I had to get out of my car on a busy street.
所以我得在繁忙的街道上下车。

1361
00:56:18.570 --> 00:56:20.870
I had to run into the side of the road.
我得跑到路边。

1362
00:56:20.890 --> 00:56:22.130
I had to find this diaper.
我得找到那个尿布。

1363
00:56:22.350 --> 00:56:23.290
I pick it up.
我把它捡起来。

1364
00:56:23.290 --> 00:56:23.890
I look at it.
我看了看它。

1365
00:56:23.990 --> 00:56:26.130
I throw it back on the ground and yell, damn it.
我把它扔回地上，大喊一声，该死。

1366
00:56:26.510 --> 00:56:27.490
Then it would have cut.
然后镜头就会切掉。

1367
00:56:28.390 --> 00:56:32.850
Then we both had driving, talking heads separate from one another.
接着我们俩分别有单独的开车访谈镜头。

1368
00:56:33.030 --> 00:56:38.430
It would have cut to Dwight's car on the interior, and he's looking in his rearview mirror saying,
镜头会切到德怀特的车内，他看着后视镜说，

1369
00:56:38.610 --> 00:56:40.530
you think I wouldn't grab a second diaper?
你以为我不会多带一个尿布吗？

1370
00:56:40.730 --> 00:56:43.830
You always have a decoy for everything, idiot.
你对任何事都有诱饵，笨蛋。

1371
00:56:44.450 --> 00:56:44.930
Amazing.
太棒了。

1372
00:56:45.670 --> 00:56:47.510
Then Angela's getting more and more frustrated.
然后安吉拉变得越来越沮丧。

1373
00:56:48.030 --> 00:56:52.550
Here's one of those moments, and by the way, this was scripted exactly as I said it.
这就是其中一个瞬间，顺便说一下，这完全是按照我说的剧本演的。

1374
00:56:53.150 --> 00:56:55.470
This is how Angela Martin curses, you guys.
各位，安吉拉·马丁就是这样骂人的。

1375
00:56:56.270 --> 00:57:00.010
Where are you going, you GD son of a B?
你要去哪儿，你这该死的混蛋？

1376
00:57:01.170 --> 00:57:01.610
H!
H！

1377
00:57:02.830 --> 00:57:04.430
So it's a lot of letters.
所以那是很多字母。

1378
00:57:04.810 --> 00:57:07.390
She doesn't say anything full out.
她什么完整的词都不说。

1379
00:57:07.610 --> 00:57:11.010
She just has all of her abbreviations that she says very angrily.
她只是非常愤怒地说出她所有的缩写。

1380
00:57:11.190 --> 00:57:17.290
One of my bosses that I worked for, who I just absolutely adored, who was so supportive of my acting career,
我以前的一位老板，我非常敬爱他，他非常支持我的演艺事业，

1381
00:57:17.470 --> 00:57:22.930
he would let me leave secretly for auditions and cover for me with the powers that be.
他会让我偷偷溜出去试镜，并帮我在高层面前打掩护。

1382
00:57:23.310 --> 00:57:25.030
I was his executive assistant.
我当时是他的行政助理。

1383
00:57:25.310 --> 00:57:29.030
When he would get really frustrated in his office, he would go,
当他在办公室里感到非常沮丧时，他会说，

1384
00:57:29.030 --> 00:57:30.830
Oh, fiddlesticks!
噢，该死！

1385
00:57:31.630 --> 00:57:33.550
He would say fiddlesticks.
他会说“该死”。

1386
00:57:33.770 --> 00:57:35.030
It was so pure.
那真是太纯粹了。

1387
00:57:35.570 --> 00:57:36.230
So cute.
太可爱了。

1388
00:57:36.450 --> 00:57:38.590
But I knew he was real upset if he said it.
但我知道如果他说了这个词，他就是真的生气了。

1389
00:57:38.710 --> 00:57:39.110
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1390
00:57:39.510 --> 00:57:40.370
I'd be like, uh-oh.
我会想，噢噢。

1391
00:57:40.610 --> 00:57:41.610
Son of a B.
该死的混蛋。

1392
00:57:42.050 --> 00:57:42.450
H!
H！

1393
00:57:42.610 --> 00:57:43.110
I know.
我知道。

1394
00:57:43.270 --> 00:57:45.370
He and Angela would make quite a pair.
他和安吉拉会是一对绝配。

1395
00:57:45.470 --> 00:57:45.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1396
00:57:46.070 --> 00:57:47.510
See them argue at home.
想象一下他们在家里争吵的样子。

1397
00:57:47.870 --> 00:57:50.890
Well, the car chase is going to end in what looks like is a dead end.
好吧，追车戏将会在一个看起来像是死胡同的地方结束。

1398
00:57:51.050 --> 00:57:52.970
In real life, it was actually a cul-de-sac.
在现实生活中，那其实是一个尽头路。

1399
00:57:53.090 --> 00:57:56.850
And I want to read from the shooting draft how this scene was described.
我想读一下拍摄剧本里是怎么描述这个场景的。

1400
00:57:57.210 --> 00:57:57.770
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

1401
00:57:57.770 --> 00:58:00.750
Angela gains on the Thunderbird, honking and honking.
安吉拉追上了那辆雷鸟，不停地按着喇叭。

1402
00:58:00.950 --> 00:58:02.170
The Thunderbird pulls over.
雷鸟靠边停下了。

1403
00:58:02.610 --> 00:58:04.010
Angela runs over to the car.
安吉拉跑向那辆车。

1404
00:58:04.450 --> 00:58:05.510
Angela, no!
安吉拉，别这样！

1405
00:58:06.090 --> 00:58:08.650
She opens the door and pulls out the driver of the car.
她打开车门，把司机拽了出来。

1406
00:58:08.950 --> 00:58:10.210
It's Moe's!
是莫斯！

1407
00:58:10.550 --> 00:58:11.290
Exclamation point.
感叹号。

1408
00:58:11.630 --> 00:58:13.350
She starts shaking him.
她开始摇晃他。

1409
00:58:13.610 --> 00:58:14.990
Angela, where is he?
安吉拉，他在哪儿？

1410
00:58:15.110 --> 00:58:16.050
Where did he go?
他去哪儿了？

1411
00:58:16.390 --> 00:58:18.510
Moe's, I'm not supposed to say.
安吉拉，我不能说。

1412
00:58:18.810 --> 00:58:20.950
Angela slaps Moe's in the face.
安吉拉扇了莫斯一巴掌。

1413
00:58:21.170 --> 00:58:22.730
Angela says, where is he?
安吉拉说，他在哪儿？

1414
00:58:22.890 --> 00:58:23.650
Where is he?
他在哪儿？

1415
00:58:24.090 --> 00:58:25.430
Moe's runs away.
莫斯跑开了。

1416
00:58:25.430 --> 00:58:27.910
We got some fan mail about this, Angela.
安吉拉，我们收到了一些关于这件事的粉丝来信。

1417
00:58:28.110 --> 00:58:29.690
Are you ready to answer some letters?
你准备好回信了吗？

1418
00:58:30.150 --> 00:58:30.430
I am.
我准备好了。

1419
00:58:30.850 --> 00:58:31.390
All right.
好的。

1420
00:58:32.010 --> 00:58:35.890
Fan mail flurry first up from Ivan N.
第一封粉丝来信来自智利的伊万·N。

1421
00:58:36.110 --> 00:58:36.570
in Chile.
在智利。

1422
00:58:37.310 --> 00:58:42.390
Angela, is that really you, driving the car in pursuit of the diaper?
安吉拉，开车追逐尿布的那个人真的是你吗？

1423
00:58:42.870 --> 00:58:43.270
Okay.
好的。

1424
00:58:43.490 --> 00:58:44.930
I will say this.
我会这么说。

1425
00:58:45.050 --> 00:58:46.270
Yes and no, Ivan.
既是也不是，伊万。

1426
00:58:46.410 --> 00:58:50.650
Because there were a lot of driving sequences, as we have shared.
因为正如我们分享过的那样，有很多驾驶镜头。

1427
00:58:50.650 --> 00:58:53.510
Anything on the big open roads, that was not us.
任何在宽阔大路上的镜头，那都不是我们拍的。

1428
00:58:53.510 --> 00:58:53.890
Okay.
好的。

1429
00:58:54.230 --> 00:58:54.450
Right?
对吧？

1430
00:58:54.690 --> 00:59:00.090
But this little sort of peeling out into the cul-de-sac, where we pull up kind of side
但这种冲进死胡同的小片段，就是我们并排停下的那种，

1431
00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:02.570
by side, Mike and I did do that.
我和迈克确实拍了。

1432
00:59:02.750 --> 00:59:05.470
But it was a dead-end cul-de-sac.
但那是一个死胡同。

1433
00:59:05.610 --> 00:59:08.950
There were no homes or businesses or anything.
那里没有住宅、商店或其他任何东西。

1434
00:59:09.110 --> 00:59:11.710
It sort of backed up like a parking lot.
它看起来就像个停车场。

1435
00:59:11.870 --> 00:59:14.940
So there was no other motorist that we could...
所以没有其他司机会让我们……

1436
00:59:15.890 --> 00:59:16.430
Accidentally...
意外地……

1437
00:59:16.430 --> 00:59:16.750
Yes.
是的。

1438
00:59:17.150 --> 00:59:17.710
Run into.
撞上。

1439
00:59:17.790 --> 00:59:18.570
...to worry about.
……需要担心。

1440
00:59:18.570 --> 00:59:23.650
But having said that, even us just pulling in and having to do the sequence where we
但话虽如此，即使是我们开车进去，不得不拍摄那种我们……

1441
00:59:23.650 --> 00:59:29.130
kind of pull in a little bit side by side, staggered, the stunt coordinator showed us
稍微并排错位停下的镜头时，特技协调员也向我们展示了

1442
00:59:29.130 --> 00:59:34.230
exactly where the car would stop, where we would pull up to, and we had a little practice
车子具体会在哪里停下，我们要开到哪里，我们在拍摄对话之前

1443
00:59:34.230 --> 00:59:36.210
before we did any of the dialogue.
还进行了一点练习。

1444
00:59:36.490 --> 00:59:38.510
I've done driving scenes like that before.
我以前拍过类似的驾驶场景。

1445
00:59:38.510 --> 00:59:44.950
We talk about as actors, sometimes in order to be on camera in focus, you have to hit a mark
作为演员，我们常说，有时为了在镜头里保持对焦，你必须走到一个标记点，

1446
00:59:44.950 --> 00:59:46.690
and they'll put a little piece of tape on the ground.
他们会在地上贴一小块胶带。

1447
00:59:46.850 --> 00:59:50.570
They'll be like, okay, when you enter this scene, you've got to stand right here or else
他们会说，好了，当你进入这个场景时，你必须站在这里，否则

1448
00:59:50.570 --> 00:59:51.510
you're going to be out of focus.
你就会失焦。

1449
00:59:52.270 --> 00:59:55.670
And then in these driving sequences, your car will have a mark.
而在这些驾驶镜头中，你的车也会有一个标记点。

1450
00:59:56.090 --> 00:59:56.450
Yes.
是的。

1451
00:59:56.610 --> 01:00:01.650
That is so hard to do, to stop your car at the exact right place.
要把车停在恰到好处的位置，这真的太难了。

1452
01:00:01.830 --> 01:00:02.110
Right.
确实。

1453
01:00:02.270 --> 01:00:03.230
And throw it in park.
还得挂上停车挡。

1454
01:00:03.410 --> 01:00:05.730
Make sure you throw it in park because then you've got to get out and run.
一定要记得挂上停车挡，因为接下来你得下车跑过去。

1455
01:00:06.090 --> 01:00:09.530
And there was a camera operator between the two cars standing there.
当时两辆车之间还站着一位摄像师。

1456
01:00:09.750 --> 01:00:10.010
Wow.
哇。

1457
01:00:10.010 --> 01:00:15.510
Well, Steve Burgess said not to give away too many secrets, but Angela had a driving stunt
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说不要透露太多秘密，但安吉拉确实有一位替身演员

1458
01:00:15.510 --> 01:00:21.370
double named Nancy Thurston, and Brett Jones was the Dwight stunt double.
叫南希·瑟斯顿，而布雷特·琼斯是德怀特的替身。

1459
01:00:21.770 --> 01:00:27.370
He was dressed up to look like Dwight, and he drove both for Rain and then also for Mike
他打扮得和德怀特一模一样，他既为雷恩开车，也为迈克·舒尔开车，

1460
01:00:27.370 --> 01:00:32.250
Schur, he sent a picture of Brett dressed up as Dwight.
他发了一张布雷特打扮成德怀特的照片。

1461
01:00:32.390 --> 01:00:33.030
It's really great.
真的很棒。

1462
01:00:33.210 --> 01:00:33.270
Awesome.
太厉害了。

1463
01:00:33.270 --> 01:00:34.770
So we can share that in our stories.
我们可以把它分享到我们的故事里。

1464
01:00:35.070 --> 01:00:38.850
And Steve Burgess said Nancy really looked like you, Angela.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说南希看起来真的很像你，安吉拉。

1465
01:00:39.110 --> 01:00:39.450
Really?
真的吗？

1466
01:00:40.010 --> 01:00:43.170
It would be, they were fooled sometimes.
确实会，他们有时候也会被骗到。

1467
01:00:43.190 --> 01:00:44.970
They were like, wait, is Angela in the car?
他们会想，等等，安吉拉在车里吗？

1468
01:00:45.090 --> 01:00:45.850
No, it's Nancy.
不，那是南希。

1469
01:00:46.410 --> 01:00:46.910
All right.
好吧。

1470
01:00:46.970 --> 01:00:48.810
Are you ready for your next fan question, Angela?
安吉拉，准备好回答下一个粉丝提问了吗？

1471
01:00:48.990 --> 01:00:49.510
I am.
准备好了。

1472
01:00:49.670 --> 01:00:50.830
This is from Grant S.
这是来自德克萨斯州奥斯汀的格兰特·S的提问，

1473
01:00:50.990 --> 01:00:53.090
in Austin, Texas, who would like to know,
他想知道，

1474
01:00:53.290 --> 01:00:58.510
when Angela smacks Moe's at the end of the car chase, did Angela really smack Mike?
当安吉拉在追车戏结尾扇莫斯耳光时，安吉拉是真的扇了迈克吗？

1475
01:00:58.930 --> 01:01:04.530
The sound makes it seem like it was a hard hit, and I'm not sure which answer I'm hoping for.
那个声音听起来打得很重，我都不确定我希望答案是什么。

1476
01:01:05.130 --> 01:01:05.950
Oh, Grant.
噢，格兰特。

1477
01:01:06.350 --> 01:01:09.050
Yes, I did slap him really hard.
是的，我确实狠狠地扇了他。

1478
01:01:09.050 --> 01:01:12.650
And that sound you hear from the slap is very real.
而且你听到的那个耳光声是非常真实的。

1479
01:01:12.890 --> 01:01:14.190
They added nothing in poSt.
后期制作中没有添加任何音效。

1480
01:01:14.330 --> 01:01:15.670
But here's the deal, Grant.
但情况是这样的，格兰特。

1481
01:01:16.150 --> 01:01:18.550
I didn't slap him in the beginning.
一开始我并没有真打。

1482
01:01:18.770 --> 01:01:21.390
We did a few takes where I did a fake slap.
我们拍了几条假打的镜头。

1483
01:01:21.690 --> 01:01:23.750
But the camera is really close.
但摄像机离得非常近。

1484
01:01:23.750 --> 01:01:26.750
If you rewatch that scene, the camera is right up on us.
如果你重看那场戏，摄像机就怼在我们脸上。

1485
01:01:26.750 --> 01:01:31.150
And they could just tell that it wasn't really having any effect, right?
他们一眼就能看出那根本没效果，对吧？

1486
01:01:32.830 --> 01:01:34.990
So we decided to go for it.
所以我们决定来真的。

1487
01:01:35.250 --> 01:01:37.090
And, you know, Mike Schur was on our podcaSt.
而且，你知道，迈克·舒尔上过我们的播客。

1488
01:01:37.290 --> 01:01:38.450
It's a fantastic interview.
那是一次非常精彩的采访。

1489
01:01:38.450 --> 01:01:42.350
If you haven't heard it, it's one of my favorite interviews we have done in this whole rewatch.
如果你还没听过，那是我在整个重温过程中最喜欢的采访之一。

1490
01:01:42.350 --> 01:01:45.990
But we did talk quite a bit about that slap.
我们确实聊了很多关于那个耳光的话题。

1491
01:01:45.990 --> 01:01:47.570
And here's what he had to say.
这是他当时说的话。

1492
01:01:48.130 --> 01:01:51.490
No, I hate it when there's like a fake slap on TV.
不，我讨厌电视上那种假打的耳光。

1493
01:01:51.810 --> 01:01:53.270
I'm sure this will be fine.
我相信这会没事的。

1494
01:01:53.410 --> 01:01:54.390
Just really hit me.
就真的打我吧。

1495
01:01:54.490 --> 01:01:54.870
It'll be fine.
会没事的。

1496
01:01:54.890 --> 01:01:55.770
I remember telling you that.
我记得我当时就是这么跟你说的。

1497
01:01:55.930 --> 01:01:56.950
Like, just really hit me.
就像是，真的打我吧。

1498
01:01:57.030 --> 01:01:57.430
It'll be fine.
会没事的。

1499
01:01:57.530 --> 01:01:57.930
It'll be fine.
会没事的。

1500
01:01:58.290 --> 01:02:04.710
I had no idea that you were a mixed martial arts professional.
我当时根本不知道你还是个综合格斗专业选手。

1501
01:02:05.210 --> 01:02:06.650
And you hit me so hard.
你那一巴掌打得太重了。

1502
01:02:06.830 --> 01:02:10.530
I really like lost my – I did not know where I was.
我当时真的……我完全不知道自己在哪里。

1503
01:02:10.630 --> 01:02:11.670
I didn't know what was happening.
我不知道发生了什么。

1504
01:02:12.070 --> 01:02:15.430
My eyes went blank and my hearing dropped out.
我眼前一片空白，听觉也消失了。

1505
01:02:15.430 --> 01:02:16.850
And I had no idea what was happening.
我完全不知道发生了什么。

1506
01:02:17.070 --> 01:02:18.210
It was wonderful.
那种感觉太奇妙了。

1507
01:02:19.810 --> 01:02:21.570
That's the take they used, thankfully.
谢天谢地，他们最后用了那一版镜头。

1508
01:02:22.350 --> 01:02:25.450
Because afterwards, also, I remember afterwards, you were like, oh, my God, I'm so sorry.
因为事后，我还记得事后，你当时说，天哪，我太抱歉了。

1509
01:02:25.510 --> 01:02:26.170
And I was like, no, no, no.
我说，不，不，不。

1510
01:02:26.270 --> 01:02:28.670
I just didn't understand how strong you were.
我只是没想到你力气那么大。

1511
01:02:29.730 --> 01:02:31.930
Oh, Angela, I remember when he told that story.
噢，安吉拉，我记得他讲过那个故事。

1512
01:02:32.170 --> 01:02:33.390
I felt so bad.
我当时觉得特别内疚。

1513
01:02:33.390 --> 01:02:39.350
And I realized I'd only ever slapped one other person, and that was Rainn Wilson and Casino Night.
我意识到我这辈子只打过另一个人一巴掌，那就是在《赌场之夜》里的雷恩·威尔森。

1514
01:02:39.870 --> 01:02:40.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1515
01:02:40.410 --> 01:02:44.930
And so I don't think I knew how to calibrate when they were like, okay, the camera's tight.
所以我不知道该怎么把握力度，当时他们说，好了，镜头要拍特写了。

1516
01:02:45.070 --> 01:02:45.950
Really slap him.
真的打他。

1517
01:02:46.410 --> 01:02:50.570
What are you supposed to do when they say really slap him except really slap him?
当他们说真的打他时，除了真的打他，你还能怎么办呢？

1518
01:02:50.570 --> 01:02:50.990
I know.
我知道。

1519
01:02:51.210 --> 01:02:51.950
And Mike was.
迈克当时也在。

1520
01:02:52.030 --> 01:02:53.910
He was like, Ange, I don't want it to look fake.
他说，安吉，我不想让它看起来很假。

1521
01:02:53.930 --> 01:02:54.590
I said, okay.
我说，好吧。

1522
01:02:55.790 --> 01:02:57.250
I still feel bad about it.
我现在想起这事还觉得内疚。

1523
01:02:57.390 --> 01:02:58.970
Was that the last take, though?
不过那是最后一条了吗？

1524
01:02:59.110 --> 01:03:01.170
Did you only have to do the real slap once?
你只需要真打那一次吗？

1525
01:03:01.330 --> 01:03:02.350
Oh, 100%.
噢，百分之百。

1526
01:03:02.350 --> 01:03:02.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1527
01:03:03.390 --> 01:03:03.830
We got it.
我们拍到了。

1528
01:03:04.010 --> 01:03:04.510
Don't worry.
别担心。

1529
01:03:05.310 --> 01:03:08.170
Also, Mike had a red imprint on his cheek.
而且，迈克的脸颊上留下了一个红印。

1530
01:03:09.030 --> 01:03:12.590
And so they had to be like, well, I guess the scene is done.
所以他们不得不说，好吧，我想这场戏结束了。

1531
01:03:12.610 --> 01:03:13.190
That's it.
就这样。

1532
01:03:13.250 --> 01:03:14.350
No more close-ups there.
那里不能再拍特写了。

1533
01:03:14.770 --> 01:03:20.250
Well, we should probably talk about what's been happening back in the office during this chase.
好吧，我们应该聊聊在这场追逐戏期间办公室里发生了什么。

1534
01:03:20.250 --> 01:03:24.650
We saw Kelly and Ravi pose for their portrait together.
我们看到凯莉和拉维一起拍了肖像照。

1535
01:03:24.650 --> 01:03:25.030
Yes.
是的。

1536
01:03:25.030 --> 01:03:26.350
They're very much in love.
他们正处于热恋中。

1537
01:03:26.470 --> 01:03:27.730
Ryan's very jealous.
瑞安非常嫉妒。

1538
01:03:28.250 --> 01:03:29.150
Ravi is smitten.
拉维被迷住了。

1539
01:03:29.490 --> 01:03:31.090
Ravi is definitely smitten.
拉维绝对是被迷住了。

1540
01:03:31.610 --> 01:03:33.470
And also, guess what, everybody?
还有，大家猜怎么着？

1541
01:03:33.470 --> 01:03:35.590
David Wallace did show up.
大卫·华莱士真的出现了。

1542
01:03:35.830 --> 01:03:35.970
David Wallace did show up.
大卫·华莱士真的出现了。

1543
01:03:35.970 --> 01:03:36.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1544
01:03:36.250 --> 01:03:37.030
He's here.
他来了。

1545
01:03:37.290 --> 01:03:44.290
He lets everyone know that Joe Bennett is liquidating Sabre, and they'll no longer be associated with that company.
他告诉大家乔·贝内特正在清算赛博公司，他们将不再与那家公司有任何关联。

1546
01:03:44.290 --> 01:03:46.590
Andy sees his moment.
安迪看到了他的机会。

1547
01:03:46.930 --> 01:03:48.990
He's getting ready for his big reveal.
他正准备迎接他的高光时刻。

1548
01:03:49.110 --> 01:03:50.250
His delicious moment.
他那美妙的时刻。

1549
01:03:50.250 --> 01:03:57.350
But he gets interrupted by some very practical questions from Stanley about, is there going to be a payroll interruption?
但他被斯坦利的一些非常实际的问题打断了，比如，工资发放会中断吗？

1550
01:03:57.790 --> 01:03:58.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1551
01:03:58.010 --> 01:04:01.950
People want more information about, you know, this whole sale.
大家想了解更多关于，你知道的，这次收购的细节。

1552
01:04:02.190 --> 01:04:02.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1553
01:04:02.850 --> 01:04:05.390
So Andy says that didn't really go how I was hoping.
所以安迪说事情的发展并没有如他所愿。

1554
01:04:05.810 --> 01:04:06.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1555
01:04:06.170 --> 01:04:07.070
He didn't get his moment.
他没能迎来属于自己的高光时刻。

1556
01:04:07.650 --> 01:04:12.750
Robert is now going to come out of the conference room, where I guess he has been, except for when there was the intervention.
罗伯特现在要从会议室出来了，我想他一直都在那儿，除了中间大家干预的那会儿。

1557
01:04:13.190 --> 01:04:13.410
Right.
没错。

1558
01:04:13.650 --> 01:04:17.350
He's going to introduce himself to David Wallace's Bob Cosimacus.
他要去向大卫·华莱士的鲍勃·科西马库斯做自我介绍。

1559
01:04:17.690 --> 01:04:18.090
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1560
01:04:18.270 --> 01:04:19.330
I was like, what?
我当时就想，什么鬼？

1561
01:04:20.050 --> 01:04:22.390
Why doesn't anyone say, what are you talking about?
为什么没人问一句，你在说什么呢？

1562
01:04:22.470 --> 01:04:23.410
This is Robert California.
这是罗伯特·加利福尼亚。

1563
01:04:23.970 --> 01:04:27.970
Also, he made a big speech at the senator's charity event.
而且，他在参议员的慈善活动上还发表过长篇大论。

1564
01:04:28.330 --> 01:04:28.950
Oh, lady.
噢，女士。

1565
01:04:29.270 --> 01:04:29.890
Amanda A.
来自北卡罗来纳州的阿曼达·A。

1566
01:04:30.030 --> 01:04:32.130
from North Carolina pointed that out as well.
也指出了这一点。

1567
01:04:32.330 --> 01:04:34.290
It was just two episodes ago.
那才不过是两集之前的事。

1568
01:04:34.750 --> 01:04:39.470
Both David and Robert attended a charity fundraiser event, and Robert was a main speaker.
大卫和罗伯特都参加了那场慈善筹款活动，而且罗伯特还是主要发言人。

1569
01:04:39.770 --> 01:04:40.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1570
01:04:40.330 --> 01:04:40.970
You know what?
你知道吗？

1571
01:04:41.090 --> 01:04:43.870
Nobody noticed David Wallace at this fundraiser.
在那场筹款活动上没人注意到大卫·华莱士。

1572
01:04:44.170 --> 01:04:46.450
David Wallace didn't clock Robert California.
大卫·华莱士没认出罗伯特·加利福尼亚。

1573
01:04:46.510 --> 01:04:48.470
People were out to lunch.
大家当时都走神了。

1574
01:04:48.710 --> 01:04:49.610
Okay, fine.
好吧，行。

1575
01:04:49.610 --> 01:04:53.010
Let's say we'll suspend belief here that they didn't cross paths.
我们就当是悬置怀疑，假设他们没碰上面吧。

1576
01:04:53.410 --> 01:04:54.390
At that charity event.
在那场慈善活动上。

1577
01:04:54.550 --> 01:04:56.010
David Wallace is a good businessman.
大卫·华莱士是个精明的商人。

1578
01:04:56.530 --> 01:04:57.910
He's buying this company.
他要收购这家公司。

1579
01:04:58.170 --> 01:04:58.370
Yep.
没错。

1580
01:04:58.650 --> 01:05:00.830
He would know who the CEO was and their name.
他理应知道首席执行官是谁，叫什么名字。

1581
01:05:01.090 --> 01:05:01.930
You would think.
你确实会这么想。

1582
01:05:02.150 --> 01:05:02.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1583
01:05:02.970 --> 01:05:12.070
Can we talk about something that we teased earlier that I think has been on both of our minds, which is Daryl and Jada having their portrait taken and then Val joins them?
我们能聊聊之前预告过的内容吗？我觉得我们俩都在想这件事，就是达里尔和贾达在拍肖像照，然后瓦尔加入了他们？

1584
01:05:12.330 --> 01:05:13.970
And holds Daryl's hand.
还牵着达里尔的手。

1585
01:05:13.970 --> 01:05:17.870
But also, I'm sure Jada's like, who's this lady?
但我也肯定贾达当时在想，这女的是谁啊？

1586
01:05:18.070 --> 01:05:19.070
Why is she in her picture?
她为什么会出现在照片里？

1587
01:05:19.810 --> 01:05:20.170
What?
什么？

1588
01:05:20.590 --> 01:05:20.910
What?
什么？

1589
01:05:21.190 --> 01:05:23.550
Would you like to hear the fan mail flurry about it, lady?
你想听听关于此事的粉丝来信轰炸吗，女士？

1590
01:05:23.990 --> 01:05:24.830
Val and C.
来自弗吉尼亚州的瓦尔和C。

1591
01:05:25.050 --> 01:05:33.170
from Virginia said, does anyone else find it odd that Daryl includes Val in her warehouse uniform in his family portrait?
说，还有人觉得达里尔在全家福里让穿着仓库制服的瓦尔加入很奇怪吗？

1592
01:05:33.680 --> 01:05:33.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1593
01:05:34.670 --> 01:05:35.330
Kiara V.
来自比利时的基亚拉·V。

1594
01:05:35.590 --> 01:05:37.410
from Belgium and Caitlin M.
和来自佛罗里达州圣彼得堡的凯特琳·M。

1595
01:05:37.510 --> 01:05:39.590
